WEBVTT

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.142 line:80%
[♪ theme music playing]

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:35.002 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:39.590 line:80%
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:00:39.673 --> 00:00:41.008 line:80%
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:00:47.848 --> 00:00:50.768 line:80%
ETA
1 HOUR

00:00:50.851 --> 00:00:51.977 line:80%
One hour.

00:00:52.811 --> 00:00:54.480 line:80%
-[engine revving]
-[phone vibrating]

00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:56.565 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:01:04.406 --> 00:01:06.575 line:80%
-[whooshes]
-[truck horn blares]

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:08.160 line:80%
-[exclaims]
-[tires screech]

00:01:09.703 --> 00:01:10.746 line:80%
[truck horn blares]

00:01:12.498 --> 00:01:14.500 line:80%
[breathing heavily]

00:01:17.461 --> 00:01:18.462 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.757 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.385 line:80%
[exhales heavily]

00:01:25.511 --> 00:01:26.512 line:80%
[grunts]

00:01:26.595 --> 00:01:27.930 line:80%
BEN

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.017 line:80%
Hey, Ben. I'm driving.

00:01:32.101 --> 00:01:34.895 line:80%
-[Ben] <i>Do you have your passport?</i>
-My passport? Uh…

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:37.856 line:80%
[inhales deeply]
It's in my room, in the third drawer. Why?

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.401 line:80%
[Ben] <i>Get your passport</i>
<i>and come to the airport.</i>

00:01:40.484 --> 00:01:42.277 line:80%
<i>We have to go to the States right now.</i>

00:01:42.361 --> 00:01:44.655 line:80%
What? What are you saying?

00:01:44.738 --> 00:01:46.824 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:01:46.907 --> 00:01:48.617 line:80%
Why do we have to go?

00:01:49.326 --> 00:01:51.036 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Come to my office.</i>

00:01:55.082 --> 00:01:59.294 line:80%
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

00:01:59.378 --> 00:02:00.379 line:20%
EPISODE 6

00:02:00.462 --> 00:02:01.672 line:20%
[line rings, disconnects]

00:02:03.007 --> 00:02:04.341 line:20%
[phone vibrating]

00:02:04.425 --> 00:02:05.801 line:20%
Hello?

00:02:05.884 --> 00:02:06.885 line:20%
Express delivery?

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:08.470 line:20%
I'll head there right away.

00:02:08.554 --> 00:02:12.182 line:20%
Ben, I just got here.
I'm going to receive my passport.

00:02:12.266 --> 00:02:15.394 line:20%
[Ben] <i>Hurry. There aren't many seats left</i>
<i>for the 7:30 flight.</i>

00:02:15.477 --> 00:02:17.521 line:20%
-[♪ music fades]
-[engine revs]

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.940 line:20%
[splash echoes]

00:02:21.692 --> 00:02:22.693 line:20%
[stammers]

00:02:23.527 --> 00:02:25.154 line:20%
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrating]

00:02:26.822 --> 00:02:29.033 line:20%
-Hey.
-[Ben] <i>Hurry up! We don't have time.</i>

00:02:29.116 --> 00:02:30.284 line:20%
I'm heading inside now.

00:02:30.826 --> 00:02:31.952 line:80%
Okay.

00:02:33.245 --> 00:02:35.497 line:80%
[♪ dramatic music playing]

00:02:37.207 --> 00:02:40.377 line:80%
HANG IN THERE!

00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:44.798 line:80%
Hello. This way, please.

00:02:46.759 --> 00:02:48.052 line:80%
DESIGNER SONG HARAN

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.471 line:80%
[line rings]

00:02:50.554 --> 00:02:52.181 line:80%
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

00:02:52.264 --> 00:02:55.517 line:80%
[flight attendant] <i>Dear passengers,</i>
<i>this is Korea Air, Flight 202</i>

00:02:55.601 --> 00:02:58.103 line:80%
<i>headed for Los Angeles</i>
<i>International Airport.</i>

00:02:58.604 --> 00:03:00.356 line:80%
<i>Please wear your seatbelts</i>

00:03:00.439 --> 00:03:04.610 line:80%
<i>and switch all electronic devices</i>
<i>to airplane mode.</i>

00:03:04.693 --> 00:03:07.029 line:80%
-[line continues ringing]
-[seatbelts clicking]

00:03:07.863 --> 00:03:08.864 line:80%
[gasps]

00:03:08.947 --> 00:03:10.407 line:80%
MISSED CALL
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:14.286 line:80%
Mr. Park, did you hear from Mr. Seonu?

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.371 line:80%
[Manjae] Oh?

00:03:17.748 --> 00:03:22.086 line:80%
<i>He said he'd take</i>
<i>the earliest flight to the US.</i>

00:03:22.169 --> 00:03:23.754 line:80%
<i>He must be gone already.</i>

00:03:24.505 --> 00:03:25.964 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[♪ music ends]

00:03:26.048 --> 00:03:27.049 line:80%
[phone buzzes]

00:03:27.633 --> 00:03:29.635 line:20%
YOUR PHOTOS ARE READY FOR PICKUP.
HOBAK PHOTO STUDIO

00:03:30.678 --> 00:03:32.721 line:80%
[Haran] <i>The project's suspended?</i>

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:35.015 line:80%
[Taeseok] <i>Producer Ben said</i>

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:38.018 line:80%
<i>there were major executive changes</i>
<i>at the US headquarters.</i>

00:03:38.102 --> 00:03:42.731 line:80%
<i>And the new decision-maker said</i>
<i>they'll halt all ongoing projects.</i>

00:03:42.815 --> 00:03:45.150 line:80%
<i>The project's up in the air right now.</i>

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.236 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.962 line:80%
-[bird chirping]
-[leaves rustling]

00:04:06.213 --> 00:04:07.214 line:80%
[wind whooshes]

00:04:07.297 --> 00:04:09.883 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:04:09.967 --> 00:04:11.635 line:80%
[Hayeong] They really left?

00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:12.845 line:80%
The entire staff?

00:04:12.928 --> 00:04:15.806 line:80%
The production team left in a hurry
after hearing the news.

00:04:15.889 --> 00:04:17.725 line:80%
I'll share any updates if I receive any.

00:04:17.808 --> 00:04:20.060 line:80%
This is just so sudden.

00:04:22.354 --> 00:04:25.232 line:80%
All animation work
will be on hold for now.

00:04:25.316 --> 00:04:28.068 line:80%
We'll start meetings
for the next season tomorrow,

00:04:28.152 --> 00:04:29.486 line:80%
so get ready.

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.113 line:80%
Team 1 meeting's over.

00:04:31.196 --> 00:04:32.865 line:80%
-Call Team 2.
-All right.

00:04:32.948 --> 00:04:35.659 line:80%
-[Raemee] Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:04:44.168 --> 00:04:46.545 line:80%
Wow. Weren't we pretty close?

00:04:46.628 --> 00:04:48.547 line:80%
He could've at least sent a message.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.466 line:80%
[Raemee sighs] His phone's off, too.

00:04:50.549 --> 00:04:52.801 line:80%
He was using
a temporary phone here, right?

00:04:52.885 --> 00:04:54.970 line:80%
Pureum, he's not using
this number in the States?

00:04:56.055 --> 00:04:58.724 line:80%
-Chan isn't coming here anymore, then?
-[Seunggyu] Hmm…

00:04:58.807 --> 00:05:00.893 line:80%
I feel like he'll come back soon, though.

00:05:00.976 --> 00:05:03.062 line:80%
[Raemee] Why? Did he tell you something?

00:05:03.145 --> 00:05:04.271 line:80%
[Seunggyu] No,

00:05:04.355 --> 00:05:07.733 line:80%
but I feel like he'll solve everything
and come back soon.

00:05:08.442 --> 00:05:12.446 line:80%
Chan doesn't seem like the type
to just end things like this.

00:05:12.529 --> 00:05:15.574 line:80%
Right. It hasn't been confirmed
that it's canceled yet.

00:05:16.492 --> 00:05:18.786 line:80%
Chan might already be pretty close

00:05:19.411 --> 00:05:21.330 line:80%
to the new person in charge.

00:05:21.413 --> 00:05:25.501 line:80%
You're right. He'll solve it straight away
and return with a surprise.

00:05:25.584 --> 00:05:28.128 line:80%
What kind of surprise?

00:05:28.212 --> 00:05:30.422 line:80%
-[♪ whimsical music playing]
-For example…

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:35.803 line:80%
What's this huge box? Fabric samples?

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.555 line:80%
-[employees scream]
-The Chan you ordered is here!

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:40.349 line:80%
[all cheering]

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.601 line:80%
Ta-da!

00:05:42.685 --> 00:05:45.187 line:80%
He could appear like a magic trick.

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.814 line:80%
[exclaims] That's possible.

00:05:46.897 --> 00:05:49.108 line:80%
That does suit him.

00:05:49.775 --> 00:05:50.985 line:80%
-[♪ music ends]
-[sighs]

00:05:51.068 --> 00:05:54.822 line:80%
Seonu Chan really is something.
He's making us laugh even when he's away.

00:05:55.489 --> 00:05:57.282 line:80%
[Raemee grumbles] Geez.

00:05:57.366 --> 00:05:58.701 line:80%
I really miss him.

00:05:58.784 --> 00:06:01.370 line:80%
[♪ slow sentimental music playing]

00:06:03.372 --> 00:06:04.623 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:06:06.875 --> 00:06:08.043 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:06:09.378 --> 00:06:10.629 line:80%
[Raemee] Hmm…

00:06:10.713 --> 00:06:11.964 line:80%
-[inhales sharply]
-[♪ music fades]

00:06:12.047 --> 00:06:15.009 line:80%
A reinterpretation
of Nana Atelier's early outfits.

00:06:17.344 --> 00:06:19.596 line:80%
Oh, my. This is going to work.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.265 line:80%
The new Haran's killing it lately.

00:06:21.974 --> 00:06:24.935 line:80%
You have digital files
of videos from the '70s, right?

00:06:25.019 --> 00:06:26.562 line:80%
I'll share them with you now.

00:06:26.645 --> 00:06:27.896 line:80%
[Raemee inhales sharply] Ah.

00:06:28.939 --> 00:06:33.152 line:80%
Okay. Then let's build on that
and do some more research…

00:06:34.611 --> 00:06:35.612 line:80%
[Raemee] Tsk.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:41.577 line:80%
I'm sure Chan will come back
in a few days, saying "Surprise!"

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:43.120 line:80%
So… [in English] Don't worry.

00:06:43.203 --> 00:06:45.914 line:80%
[in Korean] But if he contacts you
before then, tell us right away.

00:06:47.041 --> 00:06:49.793 line:80%
-What?
-Wouldn't he contact you first?

00:06:50.669 --> 00:06:52.588 line:80%
You haven't been screening your windows.

00:06:52.671 --> 00:06:54.840 line:80%
I know it's because of Chan.

00:06:55.591 --> 00:06:57.092 line:80%
I'm very perceptive, you know.

00:06:57.176 --> 00:06:58.802 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrating]

00:07:00.512 --> 00:07:02.014 line:80%
[stammers] Hello?

00:07:02.097 --> 00:07:03.223 line:80%
[Raemee] New Haran?

00:07:03.307 --> 00:07:04.642 line:80%
It's mine.

00:07:05.059 --> 00:07:06.060 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim.

00:07:06.143 --> 00:07:08.854 line:80%
I was going to visit on the weekend.

00:07:09.897 --> 00:07:12.107 line:80%
My phone doesn't seem to be ringing…

00:07:13.359 --> 00:07:15.444 line:80%
-[cell phone ringing]
-[exclaims]

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:18.781 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:07:22.201 --> 00:07:24.536 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:07:25.162 --> 00:07:26.205 line:80%
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

00:07:28.999 --> 00:07:30.250 line:80%
LOS ANGELES TIME DIFFERENCE

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:31.960 line:80%
SEOUL IS 17 HOURS AHEAD OF LOS ANGELES

00:07:32.044 --> 00:07:34.046 line:80%
It would be morning there.

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:35.881 line:80%
HAVE YOU ARRIVED YET?

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.846 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:07:53.065 --> 00:07:54.066 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:07:55.317 --> 00:07:56.360 line:80%
Darn it.

00:07:57.319 --> 00:07:58.404 line:80%
Did I fall asleep here?

00:07:59.238 --> 00:08:00.406 line:80%
What time is it?

00:08:01.407 --> 00:08:03.534 line:80%
[gasps] I must be crazy.

00:08:03.617 --> 00:08:05.619 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music continues]

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.041 line:80%
[sighs]

00:08:12.334 --> 00:08:13.544 line:80%
[grunts]

00:08:18.716 --> 00:08:19.925 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:08:25.014 --> 00:08:27.725 line:80%
-[whining]
-[♪ music ends]

00:08:28.475 --> 00:08:30.185 line:80%
[Nana] Innovative materials?

00:08:30.269 --> 00:08:31.854 line:80%
You mean using new materials?

00:08:31.937 --> 00:08:35.899 line:80%
Yes. The same beauty,
but more eco-friendly.

00:08:36.525 --> 00:08:40.362 line:80%
We'll recreate
one of our archive's 1979 silk pleated set

00:08:40.446 --> 00:08:42.656 line:80%
with fermented protein fabric.

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:46.243 line:80%
It'll be eco-friendly
and maintain its elegant mood.

00:08:46.827 --> 00:08:49.788 line:80%
Nice. Maison has been using
new materials these days, too.

00:08:49.872 --> 00:08:53.000 line:80%
We could target eco-conscious consumers
who don't buy clothes.

00:08:53.584 --> 00:08:55.002 line:80%
That's what I mean.

00:08:55.627 --> 00:08:56.712 line:80%
We can't.

00:08:56.795 --> 00:09:01.258 line:80%
Nana Atelier built its name
on silk and cashmere craftsmanship.

00:09:01.342 --> 00:09:03.302 line:80%
Using unstable, unverified materials

00:09:03.385 --> 00:09:06.472 line:80%
may jeopardize our launch schedule
as well as brand trust.

00:09:06.555 --> 00:09:09.516 line:80%
The show is meant to showcase
the brand's vision.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:12.645 line:80%
Young consumers care about
both style and sustainability.

00:09:12.728 --> 00:09:14.396 line:80%
We should adapt to the times.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.148 line:80%
It's all about
value-based consumption now.

00:09:16.231 --> 00:09:17.858 line:80%
If we don't, we'll get discarded.

00:09:17.941 --> 00:09:20.110 line:80%
Customer trust comes first for our brand.

00:09:20.194 --> 00:09:22.279 line:80%
Moving away from our premium materials

00:09:22.363 --> 00:09:24.907 line:80%
will risk losing the loyalty
of our longtime customers.

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:28.035 line:80%
I know trust is important,
but the world has changed.

00:09:28.118 --> 00:09:31.163 line:80%
A brand that doesn't change
is even more risky.

00:09:31.246 --> 00:09:32.998 line:80%
Taking a risk is more dangerous.

00:09:33.582 --> 00:09:35.167 line:80%
We already have a packed schedule.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:39.088 line:80%
It won't be wise to make a risky move
that may disrupt our timeline.

00:09:39.171 --> 00:09:40.381 line:80%
-I--
-[in English] Stop.

00:09:41.215 --> 00:09:43.258 line:80%
[in Korean] I welcome
discussions like this anytime.

00:09:44.009 --> 00:09:47.554 line:80%
Let's put some more thought into this
and discuss it again next time.

00:09:47.638 --> 00:09:49.139 line:80%
-Yes, ma'am.
-Okay.

00:09:49.765 --> 00:09:50.766 line:80%
I prepared everything.

00:09:50.849 --> 00:09:54.311 line:80%
There's something else.
I received good news this morning.

00:09:58.732 --> 00:10:00.526 line:80%
What? Do you want to perform or something?

00:10:02.027 --> 00:10:03.112 line:80%
Oh…

00:10:03.195 --> 00:10:06.407 line:80%
No, I just needed to adjust my outfit.

00:10:08.033 --> 00:10:10.244 line:80%
The pre-order stock
for the Lafayette coats

00:10:10.327 --> 00:10:12.579 line:80%
have already sold out.

00:10:12.663 --> 00:10:14.456 line:80%
-We received additional orders.
-[Sol cheers]

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:15.749 line:80%
[Raemee] That's amazing!

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:17.543 line:80%
[Sol] That's great news.

00:10:17.626 --> 00:10:20.629 line:80%
Good. Make sure everything stays on track
until they're shipped.

00:10:20.713 --> 00:10:22.047 line:80%
[Taeseok] Yes, ma'am.

00:10:26.218 --> 00:10:28.762 line:80%
-[thuds loudly]
-Hey. Was I wrong?

00:10:29.346 --> 00:10:31.265 line:80%
Using materials
that didn't exist back then

00:10:31.348 --> 00:10:32.599 line:80%
is what we call reinterpretation.

00:10:32.683 --> 00:10:33.892 line:80%
[Seunggyu] You're right.

00:10:33.976 --> 00:10:35.728 line:80%
The fermented protein fabric idea
was good.

00:10:35.811 --> 00:10:37.479 line:80%
Then why was Mr. Yeon like that?

00:10:37.563 --> 00:10:40.691 line:80%
"No. Customer trust comes first."

00:10:40.774 --> 00:10:42.818 line:80%
"We can't risk customer loyalty."

00:10:42.901 --> 00:10:44.069 line:80%
[scoffs]

00:10:45.237 --> 00:10:46.238 line:80%
What?

00:10:46.322 --> 00:10:48.324 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:10:49.366 --> 00:10:51.285 line:80%
[Hayeong clears throat]

00:10:52.661 --> 00:10:54.913 line:80%
Here's the list of outfits
for tomorrow's VIP fitting.

00:10:54.997 --> 00:10:56.457 line:80%
-Please get everything ready.
-[♪ music ends]

00:11:00.294 --> 00:11:03.589 line:80%
It's my job to bridge the gap
between the artist's vision and reality.

00:11:06.717 --> 00:11:10.637 line:80%
He cares so much about our family,
but why is he so strict with me?

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.223 line:80%
I'm not bothered at all.

00:11:18.062 --> 00:11:20.064 line:80%
She seems incredibly bothered, right?

00:11:20.856 --> 00:11:22.024 line:80%
[Sol] Totally.

00:11:22.608 --> 00:11:25.235 line:80%
But aren't disagreements like that
common during meetings?

00:11:25.319 --> 00:11:28.656 line:80%
That's what I mean.
Why is she suddenly so upset?

00:11:28.739 --> 00:11:30.324 line:80%
I don't understand the reason.

00:11:30.407 --> 00:11:31.408 line:80%
The reason…

00:11:32.159 --> 00:11:33.494 line:80%
Hmm.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.291 line:80%
[water spraying]

00:11:39.375 --> 00:11:41.210 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:11:42.169 --> 00:11:47.549 line:80%
[Raemee] <i>I'm sure Chan will come back</i>
<i>in a few days, saying "Surprise!"</i>

00:11:48.967 --> 00:11:50.386 line:80%
When did you get here?

00:11:50.469 --> 00:11:51.929 line:80%
You should've called.

00:11:52.012 --> 00:11:53.639 line:80%
Did everything go okay?

00:11:53.722 --> 00:11:54.723 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:57.559 line:80%
[staff] Excuse me?

00:11:58.519 --> 00:12:01.355 line:80%
Oh… Sorry, I mistook you for someone else.

00:12:06.819 --> 00:12:07.820 line:80%
[sighs]

00:12:09.655 --> 00:12:11.615 line:80%
Am I sleep deprived?

00:12:11.699 --> 00:12:14.284 line:20%
WAITING FOR GODOT

00:12:14.368 --> 00:12:16.453 line:80%
[♪ slow jazz music playing over speakers]

00:12:17.871 --> 00:12:20.332 line:80%
-[whines]
-Hello.

00:12:21.208 --> 00:12:22.793 line:80%
Hey, you're here.

00:12:22.876 --> 00:12:25.254 line:80%
[sighs] Is Genius still not eating?

00:12:25.337 --> 00:12:26.338 line:80%
[whines]

00:12:26.422 --> 00:12:28.674 line:80%
He doesn't seem to have
an appetite either.

00:12:29.258 --> 00:12:31.510 line:80%
-Sit. I'll make you coffee.
-Okay.

00:12:39.393 --> 00:12:40.394 line:80%
Huh?

00:12:41.312 --> 00:12:43.856 line:80%
You're not sitting
in your seat of seven years?

00:12:43.939 --> 00:12:46.483 line:80%
[sighs] I want to sit here today.

00:12:49.361 --> 00:12:50.362 line:80%
[sighs]

00:12:52.489 --> 00:12:53.574 line:80%
[Manjae sighs softly]

00:12:53.657 --> 00:12:55.826 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:12:55.909 --> 00:12:57.328 line:80%
[Manjae] It feels like there's a hole.

00:12:58.912 --> 00:13:03.292 line:80%
My heart feels so empty.
It's like wind is blowing through it.

00:13:05.002 --> 00:13:09.089 line:80%
I feel like he'll burst in any second,
shouting "Mr. Park!"

00:13:09.923 --> 00:13:13.302 line:80%
and going on and on about something.

00:13:13.969 --> 00:13:14.970 line:80%
[Manjae sighs]

00:13:17.598 --> 00:13:18.599 line:80%
[Chan] Mr. Park!

00:13:18.682 --> 00:13:19.933 line:80%
[Genius barks]

00:13:20.017 --> 00:13:21.268 line:80%
Did you have fun? Huh?

00:13:22.061 --> 00:13:23.604 line:80%
Genius. Hey.

00:13:25.689 --> 00:13:28.525 line:80%
[exclaims, grunts softly]

00:13:31.528 --> 00:13:33.155 line:80%
[humming]

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:39.620 line:80%
[exclaims disapprovingly]
You forgot your meds again, didn't you?

00:13:39.703 --> 00:13:42.206 line:80%
I really need to scold you. [chuckles]

00:13:43.749 --> 00:13:47.503 line:80%
I feel like I'll start hearing him
nag me again.

00:13:47.586 --> 00:13:49.963 line:80%
-When will he come back?
-Oh?

00:13:50.047 --> 00:13:51.507 line:80%
What? Is he here?

00:13:52.424 --> 00:13:53.425 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:13:53.509 --> 00:13:54.551 line:80%
Donggu.

00:13:54.635 --> 00:13:56.011 line:80%
Hello.

00:13:56.095 --> 00:13:59.223 line:80%
Is Chan still not back from Gyeongju?

00:13:59.306 --> 00:14:00.808 line:80%
I can't reach him.

00:14:00.891 --> 00:14:02.184 line:80%
He went to the US.

00:14:02.267 --> 00:14:03.519 line:80%
What?

00:14:05.771 --> 00:14:07.773 line:80%
[♪ music continues]

00:14:13.696 --> 00:14:14.697 line:80%
[Genius barks]

00:14:17.574 --> 00:14:18.575 line:80%
[Genius whines]

00:14:26.583 --> 00:14:27.918 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[♪ music fades]

00:14:30.713 --> 00:14:31.714 line:80%
[groans softly]

00:14:33.757 --> 00:14:34.800 line:80%
[Yougyum] <i>Hadam!</i>

00:14:36.927 --> 00:14:39.430 line:80%
Don't you usually go
to the study lounge on this day?

00:14:39.513 --> 00:14:40.723 line:80%
Yes.

00:14:40.806 --> 00:14:44.601 line:80%
It's so nice to ride a swing
after such a long time.

00:14:44.685 --> 00:14:47.479 line:80%
-[exclaims excitedly]
-How did you get any free time?

00:14:49.148 --> 00:14:51.066 line:80%
I have something to ask you.

00:14:53.736 --> 00:14:55.362 line:80%
CHA YOUGYUM

00:14:55.446 --> 00:14:58.574 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:14:58.657 --> 00:14:59.950 line:80%
[Yougyum] It's grated yam.

00:15:00.034 --> 00:15:02.411 line:80%
I did some research,
and they said it helps.

00:15:02.494 --> 00:15:03.787 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:15:04.455 --> 00:15:07.833 line:80%
Why was your tumbler
in my grandma's study?

00:15:07.916 --> 00:15:09.126 line:80%
Huh?

00:15:09.209 --> 00:15:10.502 line:80%
Oh… Well…

00:15:11.003 --> 00:15:13.672 line:80%
I ran into her a while ago in the park.

00:15:14.506 --> 00:15:17.926 line:80%
I left my tumbler behind,
and I guess she kept it for me.

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:20.095 line:80%
Grandma lied and said it was hers.

00:15:24.725 --> 00:15:27.061 line:80%
You keep bringing up my grandma
for no reason,

00:15:27.895 --> 00:15:30.022 line:80%
and you've been behaving strangely
these days.

00:15:31.065 --> 00:15:32.149 line:80%
What was first?

00:15:32.816 --> 00:15:34.360 line:80%
My grandma?

00:15:37.154 --> 00:15:38.155 line:80%
Or Han Sora?

00:15:39.114 --> 00:15:40.115 line:80%
What?

00:15:40.616 --> 00:15:42.493 line:80%
Why are you suddenly mentioning Han Sora?

00:15:45.037 --> 00:15:48.207 line:80%
Park Yeseul…
Why did she have to bring up Han Sora?

00:15:49.166 --> 00:15:50.459 line:80%
Should I give him a snack?

00:15:50.542 --> 00:15:51.835 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:15:54.588 --> 00:15:56.632 line:80%
SORA

00:15:56.715 --> 00:15:57.716 line:80%
[phone beeps]

00:15:58.717 --> 00:16:00.552 line:80%
<i>Hey, Yougyum. It's me, Han Sora.</i>

00:16:00.636 --> 00:16:02.429 line:80%
[Yougyum]
What are you doing after practice?

00:16:02.513 --> 00:16:03.764 line:80%
What about you?

00:16:05.808 --> 00:16:08.811 line:80%
Her number was saved on your phone
with a heart.

00:16:08.894 --> 00:16:10.646 line:80%
She just saved it without asking.

00:16:10.729 --> 00:16:13.148 line:80%
I only found out the day she saved it.

00:16:13.232 --> 00:16:14.483 line:80%
So you did meet her.

00:16:15.025 --> 00:16:16.026 line:80%
Well…

00:16:17.736 --> 00:16:20.614 line:80%
I did, but I actually…

00:16:20.698 --> 00:16:21.824 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:16:21.907 --> 00:16:23.283 line:80%
Hadam, it wasn't like that.

00:16:23.367 --> 00:16:25.285 line:80%
She kept following me when I told her--

00:16:25.369 --> 00:16:27.121 line:80%
"You're too young to marry."

00:16:27.204 --> 00:16:28.706 line:80%
"Quit the nonsense."

00:16:28.789 --> 00:16:31.959 line:80%
Did Grandma summon you
and threaten you or something?

00:16:32.042 --> 00:16:34.753 line:80%
Why would you say that?
You know she wouldn't do such a thing.

00:16:34.837 --> 00:16:36.588 line:80%
You and Grandma both deceived me.

00:16:36.672 --> 00:16:38.382 line:80%
What are you hiding from me?

00:16:38.465 --> 00:16:41.593 line:80%
Did she throw water at you,
telling you not to disrupt my studies?

00:16:41.677 --> 00:16:43.846 line:80%
Did you get annoyed
and decide to meet Han Sora?

00:16:43.929 --> 00:16:45.139 line:80%
Don't say that!

00:16:46.849 --> 00:16:48.934 line:80%
Don't you know your own grandma?

00:16:49.018 --> 00:16:51.186 line:80%
-Don't you know me?
-I don't!

00:16:53.897 --> 00:16:54.982 line:80%
[sighs dejectedly]

00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:59.278 line:80%
I met her to try to win
some brownie points,

00:16:59.361 --> 00:17:01.613 line:80%
and I met Han Sora
to tell her I'm marrying you

00:17:02.489 --> 00:17:04.241 line:80%
and that I'll report her as a stalker.

00:17:04.325 --> 00:17:06.201 line:80%
I told her to get lost.

00:17:06.285 --> 00:17:08.954 line:80%
That's all I said.
I only spoke to her for one minute.

00:17:09.913 --> 00:17:12.166 line:80%
It's nothing like what you think--

00:17:12.249 --> 00:17:13.375 line:80%
[Hadam] No.

00:17:13.959 --> 00:17:15.085 line:80%
I don't believe you.

00:17:16.378 --> 00:17:19.340 line:80%
I just can't believe
that you hid something from me.

00:17:19.423 --> 00:17:20.966 line:80%
[♪ slow emotional music playing]

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.468 line:80%
You feel like a stranger to me.

00:17:22.551 --> 00:17:24.928 line:80%
[stutters] What are you talking about?

00:17:27.056 --> 00:17:28.057 line:80%
Fine.

00:17:28.724 --> 00:17:31.685 line:80%
I couldn't tell you,
but that was only because of one thing.

00:17:33.979 --> 00:17:35.272 line:80%
I was afraid you'd get hurt.

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:37.691 line:80%
But how…

00:17:38.651 --> 00:17:41.028 line:80%
[sighs, sniffles]

00:17:42.279 --> 00:17:43.280 line:80%
Why are you crying?

00:17:43.364 --> 00:17:45.199 line:80%
I'm the one who should be crying.

00:17:45.282 --> 00:17:47.493 line:80%
[Yougyum] Did I not mean anything to you?

00:17:48.077 --> 00:17:49.578 line:80%
It's you and me, Hadam.

00:17:50.329 --> 00:17:52.956 line:80%
-This is just something trivial--
-Trivial?

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:54.708 line:80%
Is this trivial to you?

00:17:54.792 --> 00:17:56.210 line:80%
No, Hadam. I didn't mean--

00:17:56.293 --> 00:17:57.586 line:80%
If you were me…

00:17:57.670 --> 00:17:59.088 line:80%
[sobbing]

00:17:59.171 --> 00:18:02.675 line:80%
If people were gossiping
about me seeing another guy,

00:18:02.758 --> 00:18:05.344 line:80%
then you see his name
saved with a heart on my phone,

00:18:05.427 --> 00:18:07.304 line:80%
and I keep hiding things from you…

00:18:08.472 --> 00:18:10.140 line:80%
-Then wouldn't you--
-No.

00:18:11.058 --> 00:18:13.268 line:80%
No matter what people say about you,

00:18:14.395 --> 00:18:17.189 line:80%
I only trust what I've seen
and the Hadam I know.

00:18:18.399 --> 00:18:19.525 line:80%
That's the difference…

00:18:22.987 --> 00:18:23.988 line:80%
between you and me.

00:18:26.824 --> 00:18:28.993 line:80%
I'm sorry,
but I can't walk you home today.

00:18:35.541 --> 00:18:36.542 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:18:40.337 --> 00:18:41.672 line:80%
[Chan] Ms. Song!

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:52.516 line:80%
Oh…

00:18:52.599 --> 00:18:54.101 line:80%
It's you, Mr. Yeon.

00:18:54.184 --> 00:18:55.227 line:80%
Pardon?

00:18:55.311 --> 00:18:56.312 line:80%
It's nothing.

00:18:56.395 --> 00:18:58.564 line:80%
I just reported this to Ms. Kim,

00:18:59.315 --> 00:19:01.525 line:80%
but I got an email a moment ago

00:19:02.318 --> 00:19:03.402 line:80%
from Producer Ben.

00:19:06.822 --> 00:19:08.157 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:10.492 line:80%
[Taeseok] <i>All the other projects</i>
<i>have been canceled,</i>

00:19:10.576 --> 00:19:13.037 line:80%
<i>and it's not looking good</i>
<i>for Ben's team either.</i>

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.414 line:80%
<i>Seeing how he asked</i>
<i>to halt the collaboration,</i>

00:19:15.497 --> 00:19:17.583 line:80%
<i>it'll be difficult to resume the project.</i>

00:19:18.625 --> 00:19:20.502 line:80%
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

00:19:22.254 --> 00:19:24.965 line:80%
[automation]
<i>The number you have dialed is unavailable.</i>

00:19:25.049 --> 00:19:26.550 line:80%
<i>Please leave your message--</i>

00:19:29.094 --> 00:19:30.846 line:80%
You can use me as a friend
when you're bored

00:19:30.929 --> 00:19:32.514 line:80%
or a misunderstanding for Ms. Kim.

00:19:32.598 --> 00:19:34.308 line:80%
Just try me out as a free trial.

00:19:34.892 --> 00:19:37.853 line:80%
As soon as the three months is over,

00:19:37.936 --> 00:19:39.521 line:80%
I'll disappear without a trace.

00:19:44.193 --> 00:19:47.071 line:80%
What kind of trial
ends so suddenly like this?

00:19:54.036 --> 00:19:55.037 line:80%
[huffs]

00:19:55.621 --> 00:19:57.414 line:80%
What was that look Mr. Yeon gave me?

00:19:57.498 --> 00:19:59.500 line:80%
He's so warm and friendly
to everyone else.

00:19:59.583 --> 00:20:01.293 line:80%
Why is he so cold to me?

00:20:02.503 --> 00:20:03.921 line:80%
[crunching]

00:20:04.672 --> 00:20:05.881 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:20:06.674 --> 00:20:07.675 line:80%
[exclaims]

00:20:09.051 --> 00:20:10.302 line:80%
[sighs exasperatedly]

00:20:10.386 --> 00:20:12.179 line:80%
Everything's a mess already,

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:13.973 line:80%
and now our house, too?

00:20:14.848 --> 00:20:16.058 line:80%
Song Hayeong.

00:20:16.141 --> 00:20:17.434 line:80%
I almost slipped on this.

00:20:17.518 --> 00:20:20.813 line:80%
What? You didn't fall.

00:20:20.896 --> 00:20:24.149 line:80%
-[sighs] Just clean this up.
-I'll clean it later.

00:20:24.233 --> 00:20:25.985 line:80%
Just go do your thing.

00:20:26.068 --> 00:20:27.444 line:80%
When is "later"?

00:20:27.528 --> 00:20:29.613 line:80%
It's always when someone
cleans up after you.

00:20:29.697 --> 00:20:32.324 line:80%
Always? Why would you say that?

00:20:32.408 --> 00:20:34.576 line:80%
Do you think
I never clean up after myself?

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:38.372 line:80%
[sighs] Stop being childish
and clean up your own mess.

00:20:38.455 --> 00:20:40.165 line:80%
[mockingly] Yes, ma'am.

00:20:40.249 --> 00:20:41.667 line:80%
Song Hayeong.

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:44.795 line:80%
I'm taking a short nap,
so please be quiet.

00:20:45.462 --> 00:20:47.256 line:80%
I'm coming back in five minutes,
so clean this.

00:20:47.339 --> 00:20:49.341 line:80%
[groans] I said I'll clean it later.

00:20:49.425 --> 00:20:50.759 line:80%
You didn't even fall down.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:53.762 line:80%
What did you just say?

00:20:57.057 --> 00:20:59.184 line:20%
[Hadam] <i>Yougyum, let's talk…</i>

00:21:00.853 --> 00:21:01.854 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:21:04.106 --> 00:21:05.399 line:80%
[Haran] Say that again.

00:21:05.482 --> 00:21:07.818 line:80%
It's okay if I didn't fall down?

00:21:07.901 --> 00:21:10.237 line:80%
[Hayeong] Why are you taking
your anger out on me?

00:21:10.321 --> 00:21:11.989 line:80%
Go take it out
on the person who upset you.

00:21:12.072 --> 00:21:13.407 line:80%
Why are you picking a fight?

00:21:13.490 --> 00:21:15.075 line:80%
You're the one who caused it.

00:21:15.159 --> 00:21:18.037 line:80%
You clearly caused this,
and I'm the victim here.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:20.080 line:80%
If you're so logical,
you should've been a lawyer.

00:21:20.164 --> 00:21:22.333 line:80%
-Why did you become a designer?
-Hey!

00:21:22.416 --> 00:21:24.376 line:80%
You two are so childish.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:26.253 line:80%
Haven't you two aged at all?

00:21:26.337 --> 00:21:28.547 line:80%
Can't you be quiet for 30 minutes?

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:30.215 line:80%
If you want to fight, go downstairs.

00:21:30.299 --> 00:21:32.092 line:80%
You sleep downstairs.

00:21:32.176 --> 00:21:33.469 line:80%
Being a high school senior
isn't everything.

00:21:33.552 --> 00:21:36.013 line:80%
When did you ever show
any consideration for me?

00:21:36.096 --> 00:21:38.849 line:80%
You never did anything
to help me with my studies!

00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:41.185 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[Hadam] Forget it.

00:21:41.268 --> 00:21:43.687 line:80%
What would I expect
from such immature people?

00:21:43.771 --> 00:21:45.397 line:80%
There's no point talking to you.

00:21:45.481 --> 00:21:47.232 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

00:21:47.316 --> 00:21:48.400 line:80%
[sighs exasperatedly]

00:21:48.984 --> 00:21:50.110 line:80%
Song Hadam!

00:21:50.194 --> 00:21:52.488 line:80%
You shouldn't be so mean
just because you're angry.

00:21:52.571 --> 00:21:54.823 line:80%
Then why were you so mean to me?

00:21:54.907 --> 00:21:55.908 line:80%
You…

00:21:56.950 --> 00:22:00.079 line:80%
[sighs] Forget it. Just clean this up.

00:22:02.498 --> 00:22:03.499 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:22:06.293 --> 00:22:07.419 line:80%
Did you just…

00:22:09.421 --> 00:22:10.714 line:80%
-throw that at me?
-[Hayeong] Ah.

00:22:11.298 --> 00:22:12.466 line:80%
[in English] Sorry.

00:22:12.549 --> 00:22:15.302 line:80%
[in Korean] I was trying to clean it up,
but my hand slipped.

00:22:15.386 --> 00:22:16.845 line:80%
If you're so upset, throw it back.

00:22:19.014 --> 00:22:20.641 line:80%
-[scoffs]
-I threw it like you said.

00:22:20.724 --> 00:22:23.435 line:80%
You're not the only one
who can be stubborn, you know.

00:22:23.519 --> 00:22:25.854 line:80%
That's not being stubborn.
It's being crazy.

00:22:25.938 --> 00:22:27.439 line:80%
[♪ amusing music playing]

00:22:29.066 --> 00:22:30.484 line:80%
-Hey!
-What?

00:22:30.567 --> 00:22:31.860 line:80%
[Haran] You…

00:22:32.569 --> 00:22:33.654 line:80%
[yelps]

00:22:34.822 --> 00:22:36.824 line:80%
-[♪ music intensifies]
-[bullets whizzing]

00:22:40.494 --> 00:22:41.996 line:80%
[indistinct shouting]

00:22:48.752 --> 00:22:49.753 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:22:49.837 --> 00:22:50.838 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:22:50.921 --> 00:22:52.715 line:80%
What am I even doing?

00:23:05.686 --> 00:23:06.687 line:80%
You cleaned it up.

00:23:07.271 --> 00:23:08.272 line:80%
Yes.

00:23:10.274 --> 00:23:12.568 line:80%
Are you… going somewhere?

00:23:12.651 --> 00:23:15.029 line:80%
Yes, I'm going there.

00:23:16.155 --> 00:23:17.448 line:80%
What's with the car key?

00:23:17.531 --> 00:23:18.782 line:80%
I was about to go there, too.

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:21.577 line:80%
Should we go together?

00:23:22.453 --> 00:23:23.579 line:80%
Fine.

00:23:24.413 --> 00:23:25.581 line:80%
But just us?

00:23:26.665 --> 00:23:30.377 line:80%
E raised to the power of 3in
equals negative c plus one.

00:23:30.461 --> 00:23:32.963 line:80%
So for both sides to be equal,

00:23:33.047 --> 00:23:35.299 line:80%
-c should be 0, and d should be 1.
-[cell phone buzzes]

00:23:35.382 --> 00:23:38.385 line:80%
Then hx to the power of x is negative 2…

00:23:38.469 --> 00:23:40.888 line:80%
[Hayeong] <i>We're going to go there.</i>

00:23:40.971 --> 00:23:42.431 line:80%
<i>If you want to join…</i>

00:23:42.514 --> 00:23:48.395 line:80%
[teacher] Applying this formula
would give you x squared minus 2x plus 1.

00:23:48.479 --> 00:23:50.147 line:80%
-Did you get that?
-[scoffs]

00:23:50.230 --> 00:23:51.398 line:80%
[teacher] And…

00:23:51.482 --> 00:23:53.609 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:23:56.945 --> 00:23:58.947 line:80%
[sisters exclaiming]

00:24:00.157 --> 00:24:02.493 line:80%
[screaming]

00:24:04.828 --> 00:24:06.497 line:80%
There are people passing by.

00:24:06.997 --> 00:24:08.749 line:80%
[clears throat] It's so pretty.

00:24:08.832 --> 00:24:11.001 line:80%
The ocean's beautiful.

00:24:12.711 --> 00:24:14.713 line:80%
[screaming]

00:24:16.590 --> 00:24:17.591 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:24:20.719 --> 00:24:23.430 line:80%
-I ended things with Yougyum.
-Huh?

00:24:23.514 --> 00:24:24.598 line:80%
-What?
-Why?

00:24:24.682 --> 00:24:26.308 line:80%
Should we try talking to him?

00:24:27.434 --> 00:24:29.728 line:80%
We never argued before,

00:24:30.312 --> 00:24:32.564 line:80%
but we cried and shouted at each other.

00:24:32.648 --> 00:24:35.317 line:80%
So I can't even focus on studying.

00:24:36.318 --> 00:24:39.780 line:80%
At this rate, [sighs]
I'll mess up on the CSAT as well.

00:24:39.863 --> 00:24:42.741 line:80%
My life is ruined.

00:24:42.825 --> 00:24:44.660 line:80%
[Hayeong and Haran snicker]

00:24:45.327 --> 00:24:48.497 line:80%
Did you just laugh? This is serious.

00:24:48.580 --> 00:24:52.167 line:80%
I'm facing the biggest crisis
of my life right now.

00:24:52.251 --> 00:24:55.838 line:80%
My gosh. Arguing with your boyfriend twice
might destroy the entire planet.

00:24:57.047 --> 00:24:58.048 line:80%
[exclaims teasingly]

00:24:58.132 --> 00:25:00.134 line:80%
You were acting like a grown-up,

00:25:00.217 --> 00:25:02.052 line:80%
-but I guess you're still a baby.
-Hey.

00:25:02.136 --> 00:25:03.429 line:80%
What did you two argue about?

00:25:05.389 --> 00:25:08.183 line:80%
[hesitates] There was
a small misunderstanding…

00:25:08.809 --> 00:25:11.020 line:80%
[scoffs] It's obvious
that it was your fault.

00:25:11.562 --> 00:25:13.147 line:80%
He did something wrong, too.

00:25:13.230 --> 00:25:16.734 line:80%
You should've seen his face.
How could he look at me like that?

00:25:16.817 --> 00:25:17.818 line:80%
[sighs]

00:25:18.360 --> 00:25:21.697 line:80%
And, Hayeong,
what were you so pissed about?

00:25:24.742 --> 00:25:25.951 line:80%
I don't know.

00:25:26.827 --> 00:25:29.079 line:80%
It wasn't even anything serious.

00:25:29.163 --> 00:25:30.456 line:80%
Why did I get so upset?

00:25:31.290 --> 00:25:32.291 line:80%
It's a mystery.

00:25:32.374 --> 00:25:33.625 line:80%
What?

00:25:33.709 --> 00:25:35.961 line:80%
I know. It's weird.

00:25:36.628 --> 00:25:38.756 line:80%
Anyway, I'm fine now.

00:25:39.548 --> 00:25:40.841 line:80%
So it's a pass.

00:25:40.924 --> 00:25:42.426 line:80%
What about you, then?

00:25:42.509 --> 00:25:45.804 line:80%
What made you
throw snacks at me like that?

00:25:45.888 --> 00:25:48.599 line:80%
What? She threw snacks at you?

00:25:49.558 --> 00:25:51.727 line:80%
[exclaims] I missed a fun event.

00:25:51.810 --> 00:25:55.773 line:80%
"Everything's a mess already."
Weren't you talking about yourself?

00:25:55.856 --> 00:25:58.567 line:80%
I guess I just felt a bit upset.

00:25:58.651 --> 00:26:00.778 line:80%
What's going on? Huh?

00:26:00.861 --> 00:26:02.196 line:80%
What is it?

00:26:02.279 --> 00:26:03.781 line:80%
It's just…

00:26:04.615 --> 00:26:07.159 line:80%
My spring picnic ended too early.

00:26:07.242 --> 00:26:09.703 line:80%
Geez. What are you saying?

00:26:09.787 --> 00:26:12.039 line:80%
I hate it when people talk in riddles.

00:26:12.122 --> 00:26:13.332 line:80%
Just be straightforward…

00:26:15.084 --> 00:26:16.710 line:80%
[groans, exclaims]

00:26:16.794 --> 00:26:17.795 line:80%
It's cold.

00:26:18.379 --> 00:26:20.214 line:80%
I should stick close to you for a bit.

00:26:21.048 --> 00:26:22.257 line:80%
Let's go if you're cold.

00:26:22.341 --> 00:26:24.176 line:80%
No, I want to stay a bit longer.

00:26:25.552 --> 00:26:28.389 line:80%
[groans] Why is it so cold?

00:26:28.472 --> 00:26:30.474 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:26:31.558 --> 00:26:32.559 line:80%
[sighs]

00:26:45.864 --> 00:26:47.574 line:80%
Are you sure you're all right?

00:26:48.158 --> 00:26:49.284 line:80%
Me?

00:26:49.368 --> 00:26:50.703 line:80%
I'm fine.

00:26:50.786 --> 00:26:52.371 line:80%
I'm always fine.

00:26:52.454 --> 00:26:54.957 line:80%
I should be asking you that. Are you okay?

00:26:55.040 --> 00:26:56.041 line:80%
Yes.

00:26:56.875 --> 00:26:57.918 line:80%
I'll be fine.

00:26:58.836 --> 00:27:00.462 line:80%
And I want to be fine.

00:27:02.047 --> 00:27:03.799 line:80%
So I'm going to be okay.

00:27:04.967 --> 00:27:08.512 line:80%
All right. I hope you will.

00:27:09.638 --> 00:27:13.434 line:80%
Oh. I actually liked it
when we fought, though.

00:27:14.059 --> 00:27:15.394 line:80%
It reminded me of old times.

00:27:16.145 --> 00:27:17.187 line:80%
[Hayeong chuckles softly]

00:27:18.647 --> 00:27:20.274 line:80%
Chan's a really good guy.

00:27:21.317 --> 00:27:22.318 line:80%
Huh?

00:27:22.401 --> 00:27:25.279 line:80%
You'd normally never drink
on a business trip.

00:27:26.488 --> 00:27:29.241 line:80%
So I asked Raemee
about what happened in Gyeongju.

00:27:30.951 --> 00:27:33.871 line:80%
I'm sure Chan will get in touch soon.

00:27:33.954 --> 00:27:35.080 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:27:35.164 --> 00:27:36.332 line:80%
So let's just wait.

00:27:42.379 --> 00:27:44.256 line:80%
[Chan] <i>It's called an iridescent cloud.</i>

00:27:45.215 --> 00:27:48.677 line:80%
They say you have good luck
if you see an iridescent cloud.

00:27:49.678 --> 00:27:54.475 line:80%
You should look for iridescent clouds
in the sky, too,

00:27:54.558 --> 00:27:55.976 line:80%
instead of just vapor trails.

00:27:56.060 --> 00:27:58.312 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

00:28:03.651 --> 00:28:05.569 line:80%
I guess that was fake, too.

00:28:07.112 --> 00:28:08.405 line:80%
ADD NEW WALLPAPER

00:28:23.504 --> 00:28:24.505 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:28:25.005 --> 00:28:26.215 line:80%
It's okay.

00:28:27.299 --> 00:28:28.634 line:80%
Good morning.

00:28:28.717 --> 00:28:30.302 line:80%
[Seunggyu] It's not a good morning.

00:28:30.386 --> 00:28:31.720 line:80%
Our animation collaboration--

00:28:31.804 --> 00:28:34.056 line:80%
[sighs] I heard. It's too bad.

00:28:34.723 --> 00:28:37.351 line:80%
Je Raemee, can we do the concept meeting?

00:28:37.434 --> 00:28:38.686 line:80%
Huh?

00:28:38.769 --> 00:28:39.770 line:80%
Sure.

00:28:39.853 --> 00:28:41.397 line:80%
Then let's begin in 10 minutes.

00:28:47.277 --> 00:28:49.405 line:80%
[Sol] "It's too bad"?

00:28:49.488 --> 00:28:50.698 line:80%
That's it?

00:28:52.408 --> 00:28:55.744 line:80%
We even went on a trip
to Gyeongju together.

00:28:55.828 --> 00:28:57.579 line:80%
Doesn't she feel upset?

00:28:58.205 --> 00:28:59.206 line:20%
ARCHIVES

00:28:59.289 --> 00:29:01.375 line:20%
[Raemee gasps]
You must have cleaned out the archives.

00:29:01.458 --> 00:29:02.710 line:80%
When did you find all this?

00:29:03.210 --> 00:29:04.628 line:80%
I came pretty early today.

00:29:04.712 --> 00:29:08.007 line:80%
-I was looking through the material, and…
-[cell phone vibrating]

00:29:08.090 --> 00:29:09.299 line:80%
You can take it.

00:29:09.383 --> 00:29:10.509 line:80%
[in English] Sorry.

00:29:11.635 --> 00:29:13.637 line:80%
Hmm? It's not mine.

00:29:13.721 --> 00:29:15.139 line:80%
-[vibrating continues]
-Oh.

00:29:16.849 --> 00:29:18.100 line:80%
It's just spam.

00:29:19.018 --> 00:29:21.979 line:80%
Anyway,
although this is a reinterpretation,

00:29:22.062 --> 00:29:23.522 line:80%
I'd like a fresh twist…

00:29:23.605 --> 00:29:25.941 line:80%
One, you're really okay.

00:29:26.025 --> 00:29:28.777 line:80%
Two, you're pretending to be okay.

00:29:28.861 --> 00:29:31.238 line:80%
Which is it?
You're not even checking your phone.

00:29:31.322 --> 00:29:32.364 line:80%
You two were close--

00:29:32.448 --> 00:29:35.075 line:80%
Why wouldn't I be okay?
We haven't known each other long.

00:29:35.159 --> 00:29:37.077 line:80%
You're as cold as dry ice.

00:29:37.161 --> 00:29:39.163 line:80%
You're so cold.

00:29:39.830 --> 00:29:42.291 line:80%
I take back the 3.5 points.
You're zero points.

00:29:43.334 --> 00:29:46.211 line:80%
Anyway, if you look at these photos,

00:29:46.295 --> 00:29:49.298 line:80%
they seem pretty fresh even though
they're from 40 to 50 years ago.

00:29:49.381 --> 00:29:52.092 line:80%
So instead of struggling
to create something new…

00:29:52.176 --> 00:29:54.178 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing over speakers]

00:29:57.348 --> 00:29:59.016 line:80%
-[door opens]
-[Haran] Hi.

00:29:59.099 --> 00:30:01.310 line:80%
Hey. Come and sit.

00:30:01.393 --> 00:30:02.853 line:80%
-Do you want some coffee?
-Yes.

00:30:04.063 --> 00:30:05.981 line:20%
You're not sitting by the window?

00:30:06.273 --> 00:30:08.108 line:20%
This is my usual seat.

00:30:08.859 --> 00:30:11.362 line:80%
Wait, was I acting like I own this place?

00:30:12.237 --> 00:30:16.325 line:80%
By the way, it seems like the project
we were doing will be canceled.

00:30:16.408 --> 00:30:18.452 line:80%
Then Chan won't come back?

00:30:19.703 --> 00:30:20.746 line:80%
Probably not.

00:30:20.829 --> 00:30:23.374 line:80%
I thought I should tell you
since you've been waiting.

00:30:24.708 --> 00:30:26.085 line:80%
Then he could've told me…

00:30:36.345 --> 00:30:38.138 line:80%
CALCULUS

00:30:38.889 --> 00:30:39.890 line:80%
[sighs]

00:30:41.850 --> 00:30:44.603 line:80%
[student 1] Wow. I've never seen Yougyum
wearing glasses before.

00:30:44.687 --> 00:30:45.688 line:80%
He looks so good.

00:30:45.771 --> 00:30:48.399 line:80%
-[student 1] Right?
-[student 2] He's so handsome.

00:30:51.110 --> 00:30:54.113 line:80%
I only trust what I've seen
and the Hadam I know.

00:30:54.196 --> 00:30:56.448 line:80%
<i>That's the difference between you and me.</i>

00:30:56.532 --> 00:30:57.950 line:80%
[student 1] He's so handsome.

00:30:58.033 --> 00:30:59.868 line:80%
[student 2] I can't believe it.

00:30:59.952 --> 00:31:01.286 line:80%
[student 1] I wish I could date him.

00:31:01.370 --> 00:31:03.122 line:80%
[student 2] Gosh, I'm so into him.

00:31:05.040 --> 00:31:06.542 line:80%
[Hadam] Has his eyesight gotten bad?

00:31:06.625 --> 00:31:09.086 line:80%
It'll be uncomfortable
playing with glasses on.

00:31:11.714 --> 00:31:13.841 line:80%
What does it matter? We broke up anyway.

00:31:20.681 --> 00:31:24.143 line:80%
Here's the operations report
you asked for last time.

00:31:24.226 --> 00:31:25.561 line:80%
You're done already?

00:31:29.315 --> 00:31:30.316 line:80%
Ah.

00:31:30.399 --> 00:31:32.818 line:80%
It's too bad
the animation project got canceled.

00:31:32.901 --> 00:31:36.030 line:80%
I'm actually glad
I can focus more on our next season.

00:31:36.113 --> 00:31:38.115 line:80%
Call me if there's anything else you need.

00:31:53.672 --> 00:31:54.882 line:80%
[♪ mysterious music playing]

00:32:02.306 --> 00:32:03.307 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:32:04.266 --> 00:32:05.267 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:32:05.351 --> 00:32:07.645 line:80%
Should we bring the curve down
another 0.3 mm?

00:32:07.728 --> 00:32:11.649 line:80%
And I think we should lower the neckline
by 0.5 mm as well.

00:32:11.732 --> 00:32:12.900 line:80%
Then along the V-neck…

00:32:13.484 --> 00:32:14.526 line:80%
[Hayeong laughing]

00:32:15.152 --> 00:32:16.278 line:80%
What is this?

00:32:21.992 --> 00:32:23.160 line:80%
It's so funny.

00:32:25.037 --> 00:32:26.038 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:32:26.121 --> 00:32:29.041 line:80%
[automation] <i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>is unavailable. Please leave--</i>

00:32:29.625 --> 00:32:30.959 line:20%
[Sol] It's still turned off.

00:32:31.794 --> 00:32:33.921 line:80%
She didn't even come to work.
Where is she?

00:32:34.004 --> 00:32:37.257 line:80%
Isn't she in the storage room?
She's been going there before work.

00:32:37.341 --> 00:32:38.884 line:80%
Her bag's not in her office.

00:32:38.967 --> 00:32:40.219 line:80%
I don't think she even came here.

00:32:41.053 --> 00:32:42.930 line:80%
Oh? She sent an email.

00:32:44.974 --> 00:32:47.518 line:80%
"I'm sorry. I have to take a day off,

00:32:47.601 --> 00:32:50.396 line:80%
so I'm sharing what I was planning
to cover in our meeting."

00:32:50.479 --> 00:32:54.024 line:80%
What? Has she ever taken a day off before?

00:32:54.108 --> 00:32:55.901 line:80%
Why didn't she keep her phone on?

00:32:55.985 --> 00:32:58.278 line:80%
It's like she was determined to go AWOL.

00:32:58.362 --> 00:32:59.363 line:80%
Go AWOL…

00:33:04.868 --> 00:33:06.161 line:80%
Ms. Kim, Haran…

00:33:06.245 --> 00:33:07.579 line:80%
Knock!

00:33:08.163 --> 00:33:09.206 line:80%
[knocks on door]

00:33:09.289 --> 00:33:11.709 line:80%
Ms. Kim, why did Haran
suddenly take a day off?

00:33:11.792 --> 00:33:14.461 line:80%
She has the right to take a day off.
Is there a problem?

00:33:15.045 --> 00:33:19.008 line:80%
[hesitates] No,
but I think there's something wrong…

00:33:19.091 --> 00:33:22.803 line:80%
I'm not sure, but it was strange
how she threw those snacks.

00:33:22.886 --> 00:33:23.971 line:80%
And she said something

00:33:24.054 --> 00:33:26.640 line:80%
about her picnic ending
and everything being a mess.

00:33:26.724 --> 00:33:28.600 line:80%
You're the one who seems like a mess.

00:33:28.684 --> 00:33:30.477 line:80%
What I mean is…

00:33:30.561 --> 00:33:32.563 line:80%
Aren't you worried about her, Grandma?

00:33:33.522 --> 00:33:34.523 line:80%
No.

00:33:35.024 --> 00:33:36.900 line:80%
She's not a kid. She'll be fine.

00:33:36.984 --> 00:33:38.694 line:80%
Go. Don't bother me.

00:33:40.195 --> 00:33:43.699 line:80%
[groans frustratingly]
Where the heck is she?

00:33:52.458 --> 00:33:54.835 line:80%
Your daughter's growing up, isn't she?

00:33:57.463 --> 00:33:59.048 line:80%
LEAVE REQUEST FORM
SONG HARAN

00:34:00.507 --> 00:34:02.509 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:34:06.680 --> 00:34:07.848 line:80%
Hello.

00:34:08.974 --> 00:34:10.392 line:80%
I'll be there on time.

00:34:11.810 --> 00:34:13.854 line:80%
[in English] Yes,
we're scheduled to ship today.

00:34:14.480 --> 00:34:16.815 line:80%
If the Lafayette customers respond well…

00:34:20.903 --> 00:34:22.905 line:80%
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

00:34:26.408 --> 00:34:29.078 line:80%
[nurse in Korean] You've been
to the dementia care center,

00:34:29.161 --> 00:34:31.163 line:80%
-so we'll start with a screening test.
-Okay.

00:34:31.246 --> 00:34:32.873 line:80%
[nurse] Don't you have
a guardian with you?

00:34:34.958 --> 00:34:36.085 line:80%
No.

00:34:36.168 --> 00:34:37.711 line:80%
We'll call you when it's your turn.

00:34:37.795 --> 00:34:38.796 line:80%
All right.

00:34:40.047 --> 00:34:42.049 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:34:44.718 --> 00:34:47.221 line:80%
What? If this isn't urgent--

00:34:47.304 --> 00:34:50.265 line:80%
Didn't you confirm the Brulee Coat
as a one-button?

00:34:50.349 --> 00:34:52.267 line:80%
Yes, a one-button. Why?

00:34:52.351 --> 00:34:55.312 line:80%
The QC report for the factory
was stamped as a pass,

00:34:55.396 --> 00:34:57.564 line:80%
but there's no button in the sample.

00:34:57.648 --> 00:34:59.817 line:80%
<i>We have less than four hours left</i>
<i>before shipment.</i>

00:35:01.402 --> 00:35:04.947 line:80%
Contact the Seongsu-dong factory.
I'll be there soon.

00:35:07.032 --> 00:35:08.575 line:80%
How did I make such a mistake?

00:35:11.829 --> 00:35:14.748 line:80%
SUNYUL NATIONAL UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

00:35:16.959 --> 00:35:18.168 line:80%
[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong!

00:35:18.252 --> 00:35:19.545 line:80%
Wait, Na…

00:35:20.295 --> 00:35:22.381 line:80%
-[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong?
-[♪ music ends]

00:35:22.464 --> 00:35:23.632 line:80%
Nabong!

00:35:31.515 --> 00:35:32.516 line:80%
Nabong!

00:35:33.142 --> 00:35:34.143 line:80%
Nabong!

00:35:39.398 --> 00:35:40.399 line:80%
What…

00:35:41.108 --> 00:35:42.443 line:80%
What was she doing here?

00:35:44.445 --> 00:35:45.738 line:80%
How much time do we have?

00:35:45.821 --> 00:35:46.822 line:80%
Two hours.

00:35:46.905 --> 00:35:49.116 line:80%
This won't work.
We should negotiate postponing--

00:35:50.284 --> 00:35:51.785 line:80%
No, I'm not negotiating anything.

00:35:52.536 --> 00:35:55.414 line:80%
If I can't keep our promises,
then I'm not fit to make clothes.

00:35:55.497 --> 00:35:58.292 line:80%
I mistook it for a no-button coat,
so I'll fix this.

00:35:58.375 --> 00:36:00.377 line:80%
[♪ tense music playing]

00:36:01.712 --> 00:36:04.048 line:80%
We're adding buttons to all 70 coats.

00:36:04.965 --> 00:36:06.592 line:80%
Bring them when they're done.

00:36:06.675 --> 00:36:08.802 line:80%
I'll be checking each piece myself.

00:36:18.812 --> 00:36:20.064 line:80%
-[Nana in English] Pass.
-[manager] Pass.

00:36:22.858 --> 00:36:23.859 line:80%
[in Korean] Again.

00:36:25.110 --> 00:36:26.111 line:80%
[in English] Pass. Pass.

00:36:28.572 --> 00:36:31.075 line:80%
[in Korean] We have
an hour and 10 minutes until shipment.

00:36:35.663 --> 00:36:36.664 line:80%
[exhales heavily]

00:36:39.500 --> 00:36:40.709 line:80%
Thank you.

00:36:43.170 --> 00:36:45.673 line:80%
The shipment to Paris
has just been loaded.

00:36:45.756 --> 00:36:47.132 line:80%
-[♪ music ends]
-[all gasp, exclaim]

00:36:47.216 --> 00:36:48.592 line:80%
-What a relief.
-We did it.

00:36:48.676 --> 00:36:49.885 line:80%
I'm so glad.

00:36:49.968 --> 00:36:51.512 line:80%
-[indistinct chatter]
-[applause]

00:37:00.813 --> 00:37:01.814 line:80%
I'm sorry.

00:37:01.897 --> 00:37:04.608 line:80%
I made you work twice
because of my mistake.

00:37:04.692 --> 00:37:07.319 line:80%
If it weren't for you,
we wouldn't have made them on time.

00:37:07.903 --> 00:37:09.321 line:80%
Great job, everyone.

00:37:09.905 --> 00:37:11.865 line:80%
[employees applaud]

00:37:18.497 --> 00:37:19.957 line:80%
I'm sorry. It was my mistake.

00:37:21.125 --> 00:37:23.335 line:80%
I should have checked it
before the final sample.

00:37:23.419 --> 00:37:25.879 line:80%
That's enough. It was clearly my mistake.

00:37:26.422 --> 00:37:30.551 line:80%
And don't tell the design team about this.
There's no need to alarm them.

00:37:30.634 --> 00:37:31.885 line:80%
Yes, ma'am.

00:37:32.386 --> 00:37:33.470 line:80%
I'll drive you home.

00:37:33.554 --> 00:37:35.306 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:37:35.389 --> 00:37:36.557 line:80%
It's fine.

00:37:37.057 --> 00:37:38.726 line:80%
Treat the factory workers to a meal…

00:37:38.809 --> 00:37:41.061 line:80%
I booked a restaurant
and gave them expenses.

00:37:42.062 --> 00:37:43.063 line:80%
I'd like

00:37:43.897 --> 00:37:45.774 line:80%
to take you home today.

00:37:47.860 --> 00:37:49.403 line:80%
I just want to walk for a bit.

00:37:50.070 --> 00:37:51.155 line:80%
You can go.

00:38:03.459 --> 00:38:04.543 line:80%
[sighs]

00:38:12.509 --> 00:38:13.510 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

00:38:16.430 --> 00:38:20.392 line:80%
[Taeseok] <i>Whatever it is, I don't want you</i>
<i>to bear everything on your own.</i>

00:38:21.143 --> 00:38:23.062 line:80%
<i>You can tell me anything, Ms. Kim.</i>

00:38:42.247 --> 00:38:44.249 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music continuing]

00:38:51.590 --> 00:38:55.469 line:80%
Hey, Hadam. Is Haran home?
She didn't call either?

00:38:56.136 --> 00:38:57.388 line:80%
[sighs]

00:38:57.471 --> 00:39:01.433 line:80%
I'm on my way home,
but there's a lot of traffic…

00:39:04.228 --> 00:39:05.229 line:80%
Huh?

00:39:05.312 --> 00:39:06.730 line:80%
Hang on.

00:39:13.988 --> 00:39:15.406 line:80%
Was I mistaken?

00:39:24.456 --> 00:39:25.666 line:80%
[door opens]

00:39:29.169 --> 00:39:31.296 line:80%
Huh? Why are they sleeping here?

00:39:31.922 --> 00:39:33.132 line:80%
Shh.

00:39:34.633 --> 00:39:35.634 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:39:36.427 --> 00:39:38.595 line:80%
[Nana] They passed out
while waiting for you.

00:39:39.555 --> 00:39:41.932 line:80%
[sighs] So I was the culprit.

00:39:47.229 --> 00:39:49.565 line:80%
It's late. Go and get some sleep.

00:39:51.525 --> 00:39:52.568 line:80%
Good night.

00:39:58.949 --> 00:40:00.409 line:80%
But why aren't you asking

00:40:01.118 --> 00:40:04.038 line:80%
why I took the day off
or what I did all day?

00:40:04.121 --> 00:40:05.414 line:80%
You're here, so it's fine.

00:40:05.998 --> 00:40:08.208 line:80%
But next time,
write a proper form when taking a leave.

00:40:09.752 --> 00:40:11.170 line:80%
It's not an art class, you know.

00:40:11.962 --> 00:40:14.089 line:80%
Don't scribble on the request form.

00:40:14.173 --> 00:40:16.175 line:80%
[hesitates] It wasn't a joke…

00:40:16.258 --> 00:40:17.676 line:80%
A butterfly knot.

00:40:18.844 --> 00:40:20.971 line:80%
You needed time to get some closure…

00:40:21.805 --> 00:40:23.223 line:80%
on Seonu Chan.

00:40:25.267 --> 00:40:27.811 line:80%
Normally, you'd never
go on a business trip a day early.

00:40:27.895 --> 00:40:31.023 line:80%
And the expressions on your face
in the videos…

00:40:32.358 --> 00:40:35.569 line:80%
I guess… you grew more attached to him
than I thought,

00:40:36.236 --> 00:40:38.197 line:80%
seeing how you needed time for closure.

00:40:40.908 --> 00:40:41.909 line:80%
I just…

00:40:42.701 --> 00:40:44.912 line:80%
wanted to be okay.

00:40:47.998 --> 00:40:50.292 line:80%
When we first met, he told me

00:40:51.585 --> 00:40:55.047 line:80%
that it seemed like
I was trapped in winter.

00:40:56.382 --> 00:40:57.424 line:80%
[Pureum] Thank you.

00:40:57.508 --> 00:40:58.676 line:80%
-[Hayeong] Thank you for these.
-[Seunggyu] Enjoy.

00:40:58.759 --> 00:40:59.927 line:80%
[mouthing] Thank you.

00:41:00.177 --> 00:41:02.262 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:41:03.806 --> 00:41:06.809 line:80%
Don't you crave croissants
when you see the crescent moon?

00:41:06.892 --> 00:41:11.105 line:80%
[Haran] <i>I didn't want to get trapped</i>
<i>in winter again, so I wanted to be okay,</i>

00:41:11.730 --> 00:41:14.066 line:80%
<i>but it didn't go well.</i>

00:41:16.443 --> 00:41:17.987 line:80%
I forgot to buy this.

00:41:18.070 --> 00:41:19.822 line:80%
It's my favorite. [chuckles softly]

00:41:19.905 --> 00:41:21.156 line:80%
Take this.

00:41:22.574 --> 00:41:24.451 line:80%
<i>Whatever I do, whatever I see,</i>

00:41:25.536 --> 00:41:27.246 line:80%
<i>I keep getting reminded of him.</i>

00:41:28.038 --> 00:41:30.582 line:80%
There are 0.3, 0.4, 5, 6,

00:41:30.666 --> 00:41:33.460 line:80%
oil-based, water-based,
nib tip, and ballpoint pens.

00:41:34.962 --> 00:41:36.964 line:80%
SEONU CHAN

00:41:37.047 --> 00:41:38.424 line:80%
[sighs]

00:41:38.507 --> 00:41:43.053 line:80%
[Haran] <i>I couldn't figure out</i>
<i>a way to be okay,</i>

00:41:44.221 --> 00:41:45.723 line:80%
<i>but then I found this.</i>

00:41:46.724 --> 00:41:48.267 line:20%
SEOUL DESTINATIONS LIST

00:41:48.350 --> 00:41:50.561 line:80%
Choose where to go first
so we can go together later.

00:41:51.812 --> 00:41:55.774 line:80%
[Haran] <i>So I thought I'd have some closure</i>
<i>if I checked off the whole list.</i>

00:41:56.400 --> 00:42:01.155 line:80%
<i>-This could be the final knot.</i>
-[indistinct chatter]

00:42:01.238 --> 00:42:02.406 line:80%
-[student 1] What about this?
-[student 2] This?

00:42:02.489 --> 00:42:04.825 line:80%
-[student 3] Can I try this?
-[student 4] It looks good on you.

00:42:06.327 --> 00:42:08.579 line:80%
How should I choose?

00:42:13.042 --> 00:42:15.836 line:80%
Sorry, but could you take a photo of us?

00:42:15.919 --> 00:42:16.920 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:42:17.004 --> 00:42:18.005 line:80%
-We'll take one for you, too.
-Thank you.

00:42:18.088 --> 00:42:19.298 line:80%
Oh, I'm okay.

00:42:19.381 --> 00:42:20.549 line:80%
[woman] Thank you.

00:42:21.842 --> 00:42:24.386 line:80%
[Haran] <i>So I went sightseeing</i>
<i>here and there</i>

00:42:24.470 --> 00:42:26.639 line:80%
<i>and tried a lot of things…</i>

00:42:26.722 --> 00:42:28.724 line:80%
[lively chatter]

00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:39.526 line:80%
<i>But I kept feeling bored, for some reason.</i>

00:42:40.778 --> 00:42:46.367 line:80%
<i>Everything I did with him</i>
<i>was just so fun and exciting,</i>

00:42:47.242 --> 00:42:50.329 line:80%
so I thought it would be fun
to do whatever was on the list.

00:42:53.207 --> 00:42:54.333 line:80%
Haran.

00:42:56.043 --> 00:42:59.880 line:80%
People, relationships, and even memories

00:42:59.963 --> 00:43:03.801 line:80%
could disappear tomorrow
if you let them slip through your hands.

00:43:04.802 --> 00:43:06.720 line:80%
Go to the US and see him.

00:43:07.304 --> 00:43:09.848 line:80%
Whether you become okay or not,
get it sorted.

00:43:09.932 --> 00:43:12.017 line:80%
You can easily meet him if you want to.

00:43:13.227 --> 00:43:17.272 line:80%
No, we were never that close
to begin with.

00:43:17.356 --> 00:43:18.482 line:80%
That would be silly.

00:43:18.565 --> 00:43:24.363 line:80%
There's nothing as sad and stupid
as regretting things

00:43:25.239 --> 00:43:26.949 line:80%
after time has passed.

00:43:27.032 --> 00:43:30.035 line:80%
Life is too short
to spend it on regretting things.

00:43:31.078 --> 00:43:33.622 line:80%
He was going to go back anyway.

00:43:34.248 --> 00:43:35.833 line:80%
He just left earlier than planned.

00:43:37.334 --> 00:43:38.335 line:80%
[Haran sighs]

00:43:38.419 --> 00:43:40.963 line:80%
This is why I didn't want
to get close to anyone.

00:43:41.046 --> 00:43:42.381 line:80%
So do you regret it?

00:43:43.924 --> 00:43:47.386 line:80%
Do you regret getting to know Mr. Seonu?

00:43:50.431 --> 00:43:51.473 line:80%
I do…

00:43:52.850 --> 00:43:53.976 line:80%
have regrets.

00:43:55.394 --> 00:43:57.354 line:80%
If I knew he'd leave so quickly,

00:43:57.938 --> 00:43:59.148 line:80%
I would have been…

00:44:01.150 --> 00:44:02.192 line:80%
kinder to him.

00:44:02.276 --> 00:44:04.278 line:80%
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:44:05.237 --> 00:44:07.740 line:80%
I was a bit mean to him at first.

00:44:09.241 --> 00:44:11.994 line:80%
But I don't regret

00:44:13.370 --> 00:44:14.747 line:80%
getting to know him.

00:44:15.331 --> 00:44:16.540 line:80%
A three-month trial!

00:44:16.623 --> 00:44:17.958 line:80%
There's nothing to lose.

00:44:18.042 --> 00:44:19.752 line:80%
You can overcome it.

00:44:19.835 --> 00:44:21.503 line:80%
Once you know how,

00:44:22.296 --> 00:44:24.590 line:80%
you'll be able to escape on your own.

00:44:25.299 --> 00:44:30.262 line:80%
I learned it through that person,
so I wanted to show you, too.

00:44:30.846 --> 00:44:32.765 line:80%
Thanks to that weird trial,

00:44:34.183 --> 00:44:36.518 line:80%
I learned how to escape on my own.

00:44:39.521 --> 00:44:42.232 line:80%
So I know I met a great person.

00:44:45.235 --> 00:44:46.820 line:80%
I feel grateful.

00:44:49.406 --> 00:44:51.617 line:80%
Then that's enough. [chuckles softly]

00:45:08.676 --> 00:45:11.970 line:80%
[Nana] <i>Traditional knots</i>
<i>each have a specific meaning.</i>

00:45:13.138 --> 00:45:15.933 line:80%
<i>A new life, change…</i>

00:45:16.016 --> 00:45:19.561 line:80%
<i>Sometimes, you have to free something</i>
<i>instead of clutching it tightly</i>

00:45:19.645 --> 00:45:21.313 line:80%
<i>to open up a new beginning.</i>

00:45:21.981 --> 00:45:25.192 line:80%
<i>That's what… this butterfly knot means.</i>

00:45:34.702 --> 00:45:35.703 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

00:45:39.123 --> 00:45:41.333 line:80%
Is she not coming today either?

00:45:42.334 --> 00:45:45.045 line:80%
Sorry, I'm late.
It took some time picking up bribes.

00:45:45.129 --> 00:45:46.714 line:80%
-She's here.
-Ms. Song.

00:45:46.797 --> 00:45:48.882 line:80%
I was late helping her carry this.

00:45:48.966 --> 00:45:50.175 line:80%
[Sol exclaims excitedly]

00:45:51.218 --> 00:45:53.637 line:80%
This is an apology
for taking a leave without notice.

00:45:53.721 --> 00:45:56.098 line:80%
-[Sol and Pureum] Thanks.
-[Seunggyu] Thank you.

00:45:56.181 --> 00:45:57.558 line:80%
Didn't you bring mine?

00:45:58.142 --> 00:45:59.685 line:80%
Of course, we did.

00:45:59.768 --> 00:46:00.978 line:80%
[Nana chuckles softly]

00:46:01.478 --> 00:46:04.732 line:80%
Someone go visit Mr. Yoon's exhibit later.
I have plans today.

00:46:05.190 --> 00:46:06.191 line:80%
I'll go.

00:46:08.819 --> 00:46:11.155 line:80%
All right. Go and visit him.

00:46:12.364 --> 00:46:14.033 line:80%
-Thanks for the coffee.
-Sure.

00:46:16.076 --> 00:46:17.077 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

00:46:17.161 --> 00:46:19.079 line:80%
-[Seunggyu] Thank you.
-[Raemee in English] Thank you.

00:46:19.163 --> 00:46:20.497 line:80%
[Manjae in Korean]
<i>Drop by when you're free.</i>

00:46:20.581 --> 00:46:22.541 line:80%
<i>There's another thing</i>
<i>waiting for its owner.</i>

00:46:28.714 --> 00:46:29.715 line:80%
[knock on door]

00:46:29.798 --> 00:46:30.799 line:80%
Yes?

00:46:32.217 --> 00:46:34.428 line:80%
[sighs softly] I'll go with you.

00:46:34.511 --> 00:46:37.264 line:80%
I thought you'd return
to your cold, distant self.

00:46:37.348 --> 00:46:38.515 line:80%
I'm proud of you.

00:46:42.227 --> 00:46:43.228 line:80%
[door closes]

00:46:44.521 --> 00:46:45.689 line:80%
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:46:45.773 --> 00:46:46.815 line:80%
[Manjae] Here.

00:46:47.775 --> 00:46:49.193 line:80%
What is it this time?

00:46:49.276 --> 00:46:51.695 line:80%
Did you find a flower ring
you were going to give me?

00:46:53.405 --> 00:46:55.991 line:80%
I saw you when I was getting my checkup.

00:46:58.744 --> 00:47:00.162 line:80%
Why were you at the hospital?

00:47:00.245 --> 00:47:01.664 line:80%
Are you sick or anything?

00:47:01.747 --> 00:47:04.583 line:80%
I was just visiting a friend there.

00:47:04.667 --> 00:47:08.003 line:80%
Then what made you rush out like that?
You even dropped your hat.

00:47:09.380 --> 00:47:13.425 line:80%
Something urgent came up at work,
so, of course, I wasn't skipping happily.

00:47:14.301 --> 00:47:15.302 line:80%
[sighs]

00:47:16.595 --> 00:47:17.846 line:80%
Oh, right.

00:47:17.930 --> 00:47:20.265 line:80%
Seonu Chan
didn't contact you either, did he?

00:47:20.933 --> 00:47:21.934 line:80%
What?

00:47:23.018 --> 00:47:26.730 line:80%
No, he didn't.
I'm actually worried about Haran, though.

00:47:27.439 --> 00:47:29.942 line:80%
There seemed to be something
going on between them.

00:47:30.025 --> 00:47:33.529 line:80%
I'm worried she'll end up in pain
like seven years ago.

00:47:34.113 --> 00:47:35.447 line:80%
It won't happen again.

00:47:35.531 --> 00:47:38.158 line:80%
She seems to have grown stronger
after spending time with him.

00:47:38.742 --> 00:47:41.954 line:80%
Right. My roommate
was quite an incredible guy.

00:47:44.373 --> 00:47:45.708 line:80%
I feel really grateful.

00:47:46.291 --> 00:47:47.751 line:80%
It's such a shame.

00:47:51.964 --> 00:47:53.173 line:80%
-[sighs]
-[♪ music fades]

00:47:54.091 --> 00:47:55.968 line:80%
I loved the exhibit.

00:47:57.177 --> 00:47:58.679 line:80%
Gosh, look at all these people.

00:47:58.762 --> 00:48:02.182 line:80%
Being out here on a bustling street
makes me so excited!

00:48:02.266 --> 00:48:03.309 line:80%
[both chuckle]

00:48:03.392 --> 00:48:04.393 line:80%
[cell phone buzzes]

00:48:08.605 --> 00:48:10.482 line:80%
7:00 P.M. SAMCHEONG-DONG
TODAY 7:00 P.M.

00:48:10.566 --> 00:48:12.735 line:80%
[Chan] <i>Ah. Mark that on your schedule.</i>

00:48:12.818 --> 00:48:14.653 line:80%
<i>You'd better not forget or show up late.</i>

00:48:18.365 --> 00:48:19.908 line:80%
I totally forgot about this.

00:48:19.992 --> 00:48:21.827 line:20%
Can't I cancel it?

00:48:24.455 --> 00:48:25.456 line:80%
[in English] Oh, God!

00:48:25.539 --> 00:48:27.875 line:80%
[in Korean] Isn't this restaurant
so, so, so famous

00:48:27.958 --> 00:48:31.837 line:80%
that you have to wait for months
to book a table?

00:48:33.005 --> 00:48:34.465 line:80%
Take me instead of canceling.

00:48:35.215 --> 00:48:37.176 line:80%
[hesitates] There isn't much time left…

00:48:37.259 --> 00:48:38.844 line:80%
It's just right over there.

00:48:38.927 --> 00:48:41.013 line:80%
We can get there if we run.

00:48:41.096 --> 00:48:43.432 line:80%
-[stutters]
-[Raemee] Come on!

00:48:44.058 --> 00:48:46.060 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:48:49.438 --> 00:48:50.439 line:80%
This is amazing.

00:48:51.732 --> 00:48:53.651 line:80%
It's so nice and peaceful here.

00:48:53.734 --> 00:48:56.278 line:80%
[♪ soft piano music playing over speakers]

00:48:56.987 --> 00:48:58.322 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

00:48:58.405 --> 00:49:00.032 line:80%
[camera clicking]

00:49:02.368 --> 00:49:03.369 line:80%
Yes, Ms. Kim.

00:49:04.036 --> 00:49:05.579 line:80%
Yes, I saw him.

00:49:07.122 --> 00:49:09.416 line:20%
I took a pamphlet, too.

00:49:09.500 --> 00:49:10.542 line:80%
[camera clicks]

00:49:10.626 --> 00:49:11.877 line:80%
[cell phone rings]

00:49:11.960 --> 00:49:12.961 line:80%
[Haran] All right.

00:49:13.796 --> 00:49:14.922 line:80%
Hello?

00:49:15.798 --> 00:49:17.466 line:80%
Really? Okay.

00:49:19.259 --> 00:49:21.136 line:80%
I'm really sorry.

00:49:21.220 --> 00:49:24.848 line:80%
My partner's a soldier,
and he just got an unexpected leave.

00:49:24.932 --> 00:49:27.935 line:80%
-So, I'm sorry, but I have to go.
-What?

00:49:28.018 --> 00:49:29.186 line:80%
Enjoy your meal. Bye.

00:49:29.269 --> 00:49:30.688 line:80%
I'm very sorry!

00:49:30.771 --> 00:49:32.439 line:80%
What…

00:49:32.523 --> 00:49:33.899 line:80%
Wait, your scarf…

00:49:34.525 --> 00:49:35.693 line:80%
Je Raemee!

00:49:35.776 --> 00:49:37.528 line:80%
Wait! [pants]

00:49:37.611 --> 00:49:39.947 line:80%
[stutters] Je Raemee, here!

00:49:40.030 --> 00:49:41.031 line:80%
Your scarf…

00:49:41.115 --> 00:49:42.700 line:80%
Give it to me next time.
[in English] Sorry!

00:49:43.534 --> 00:49:45.369 line:80%
[exclaims, sighs]

00:49:46.787 --> 00:49:48.998 line:80%
-[woman in Korean] I'm sorry.
-It's okay, I'll do it.

00:49:49.665 --> 00:49:51.250 line:80%
-Sorry.
-No problem.

00:49:52.376 --> 00:49:53.377 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:49:55.838 --> 00:49:56.839 line:80%
[sighs]

00:49:58.173 --> 00:49:59.174 line:80%
[sighs heavily]

00:49:59.258 --> 00:50:00.759 line:80%
Why did I even come here?

00:50:03.053 --> 00:50:04.054 line:80%
[sighs]

00:50:11.729 --> 00:50:14.356 line:80%
-[laughter]
-[lively chatter]

00:50:14.440 --> 00:50:16.567 line:80%
[sighs] It's even snowing?

00:50:25.451 --> 00:50:26.660 line:80%
[Chan] Ms. Song!

00:50:28.912 --> 00:50:29.913 line:80%
[sighs]

00:50:31.248 --> 00:50:32.458 line:80%
Hearing things again?

00:50:33.083 --> 00:50:34.084 line:80%
[sighs wearily]

00:50:37.212 --> 00:50:38.255 line:80%
[Chan] Ms. Song!

00:50:49.808 --> 00:50:51.894 line:80%
[footsteps echo]

00:50:51.977 --> 00:50:53.937 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

00:50:55.564 --> 00:50:57.566 line:80%
[Chan panting]

00:51:04.156 --> 00:51:05.157 line:80%
[sighs]

00:51:07.951 --> 00:51:09.161 line:80%
How have you been?

00:51:10.245 --> 00:51:12.081 line:80%
[Chan continues panting]

00:51:13.999 --> 00:51:16.418 line:80%
I told you not to be late, but I'm late.

00:51:18.921 --> 00:51:21.048 line:80%
Oh? Why do you look so frail?

00:51:22.007 --> 00:51:23.801 line:80%
Did you not eat well?

00:51:24.635 --> 00:51:25.969 line:80%
Has work been tough?

00:51:28.138 --> 00:51:29.431 line:80%
[inhales sharply]

00:51:30.099 --> 00:51:32.226 line:80%
Um… Well…

00:51:32.768 --> 00:51:34.186 line:80%
Aren't you happy to see me?

00:51:34.269 --> 00:51:36.105 line:80%
I'm so happy that I almost hugged…

00:51:38.857 --> 00:51:39.858 line:80%
I mean…

00:51:39.942 --> 00:51:41.151 line:80%
[mumbles]

00:51:41.610 --> 00:51:43.862 line:80%
[exclaims] I almost did a backflip.

00:51:43.946 --> 00:51:44.947 line:80%
[chuckles]

00:51:46.991 --> 00:51:48.492 line:80%
Here. How about a high five instead?

00:51:48.575 --> 00:51:51.203 line:80%
I usually do high fives
when I'm happy to see someone.

00:52:15.436 --> 00:52:17.021 line:80%
I have a habit…

00:52:18.230 --> 00:52:20.065 line:80%
of hugging people I'm happy to see.

00:52:39.335 --> 00:52:43.839 line:80%
I promised that I'd be here by today,
no matter what.

00:52:47.426 --> 00:52:48.427 line:80%
[sighs]

00:52:58.270 --> 00:52:59.271 line:80%
[♪ song fades]

00:52:59.355 --> 00:53:01.690 line:80%
You messaged me? When?

00:53:01.774 --> 00:53:04.526 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Didn't you come here
because of my message?

00:53:07.029 --> 00:53:09.156 line:80%
-[seatbelt sign beeps]
-[attendant] <i>Please wear your seatbelts</i>

00:53:09.239 --> 00:53:13.077 line:80%
<i>and switch all electronic devices</i>
<i>to airplane mode.</i>

00:53:15.329 --> 00:53:16.330 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I'll be back soon.</i>

00:53:16.413 --> 00:53:18.540 line:80%
<i>Even if the project gets canceled,</i>
<i>I'll be back soon.</i>

00:53:18.624 --> 00:53:20.417 line:80%
<i>We said we'd have dinner together.</i>

00:53:20.501 --> 00:53:21.710 line:80%
<i>I promise to be there by that day.</i>

00:53:21.794 --> 00:53:23.462 line:80%
<i>Don't worry even if you can't reach me.</i>

00:53:23.545 --> 00:53:25.714 line:80%
<i>Tell Mr. Park and everyone not to worry.</i>

00:53:25.798 --> 00:53:27.174 line:80%
Sir, we'll be taking off soon.

00:53:27.257 --> 00:53:29.051 line:80%
-Please switch to airplane mode.
-Okay.

00:53:29.134 --> 00:53:31.053 line:80%
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

00:53:33.305 --> 00:53:35.557 line:80%
-[cell phone vibrates]
-It's on.

00:53:35.641 --> 00:53:36.642 line:80%
Oh.

00:53:37.601 --> 00:53:38.686 line:80%
Look, I sent it…

00:53:38.769 --> 00:53:41.271 line:80%
Oh? What's this exclamation mark?

00:53:42.606 --> 00:53:43.857 line:80%
[sighs]

00:53:43.941 --> 00:53:45.818 line:80%
-It means it failed to send.
-[sighs]

00:53:47.361 --> 00:53:51.323 line:80%
Oh! If you didn't receive
my message, then you must have…

00:53:51.407 --> 00:53:53.909 line:80%
You're here, so it's fine. Eat up.

00:53:55.369 --> 00:53:57.454 line:80%
[sighs softly]

00:54:00.958 --> 00:54:02.209 line:80%
Have more of this.

00:54:03.544 --> 00:54:04.753 line:80%
[Chan grunts]

00:54:07.464 --> 00:54:09.008 line:80%
Here.

00:54:10.634 --> 00:54:11.969 line:80%
Eat all of that, okay?

00:54:12.052 --> 00:54:13.762 line:80%
-This is why you're so thin.
-[♪ music fades]

00:54:13.846 --> 00:54:17.516 line:80%
Are there no mirrors in the States?
You're the one who looks so gaunt.

00:54:18.100 --> 00:54:20.936 line:80%
[exclaims teasingly]
I should've dressed up a bit.

00:54:21.603 --> 00:54:23.022 line:80%
It's been a while since we met.

00:54:23.105 --> 00:54:24.106 line:80%
[Chan clears throat]

00:54:25.649 --> 00:54:27.109 line:80%
What about headquarters?

00:54:27.192 --> 00:54:29.528 line:80%
Mr. Yeon said it's not looking so good.

00:54:30.154 --> 00:54:31.363 line:80%
Oh, um…

00:54:32.781 --> 00:54:35.743 line:80%
[hesitates] I'm not sure
how to tell you this,

00:54:36.702 --> 00:54:38.579 line:80%
-but…
-It got canceled, right?

00:54:39.330 --> 00:54:41.749 line:80%
[sighs] Then do you have to go back soon?

00:54:42.916 --> 00:54:46.045 line:80%
[inhales sharply, hesitates]
This is really important, so…

00:54:49.882 --> 00:54:52.801 line:80%
I resolved everything really well.

00:54:53.969 --> 00:54:56.472 line:80%
[♪ pensive music playing]

00:54:56.555 --> 00:54:58.390 line:80%
[stutters, sighs in relief]

00:54:59.141 --> 00:55:01.226 line:80%
It's me, Seonu Chan. [laughs]

00:55:01.310 --> 00:55:03.228 line:80%
[in English]
We've already visited the site.

00:55:03.312 --> 00:55:04.730 line:80%
Seeing it in person, it's clear

00:55:04.813 --> 00:55:07.107 line:80%
we can take this project
beyond the original idea.

00:55:07.191 --> 00:55:09.985 line:80%
If anything needs adjusting,
we can move on it right away.

00:55:10.069 --> 00:55:11.445 line:80%
No.

00:55:11.528 --> 00:55:14.448 line:80%
[Chan in Korean]
<i>It almost got canceled, but…</i>

00:55:15.366 --> 00:55:18.702 line:80%
[in English] I think Scene 27 feels
a bit flat. What do you think?

00:55:18.786 --> 00:55:21.997 line:80%
I don't think it's about the sharpness,
it's about the keyframe timing.

00:55:22.081 --> 00:55:25.376 line:80%
I don't think it's about impact.
The emotion isn't just coming through.

00:55:25.459 --> 00:55:28.545 line:80%
[Chan in Korean]
<i>Emergency meetings, back-to-back meetings,</i>

00:55:28.629 --> 00:55:31.006 line:80%
<i>persuasion, even script revisions…</i>

00:55:32.675 --> 00:55:35.386 line:80%
[in English] Hey, uh…
how's the background coming along?

00:55:36.470 --> 00:55:40.057 line:80%
Around 60 percent. But they want
another look at the main character.

00:55:40.140 --> 00:55:41.517 line:80%
-At this point?
-[employee] Yeah.

00:55:41.600 --> 00:55:42.935 line:80%
[Ben sighs dejectedly]

00:55:45.437 --> 00:55:46.438 line:80%
[sighs]

00:55:49.817 --> 00:55:50.818 line:80%
Thank you.

00:55:50.901 --> 00:55:53.237 line:80%
-[Chan grunts, inhales sharply]
-[phone rings]

00:55:53.320 --> 00:55:54.697 line:80%
[Ben] Yeah?

00:55:55.698 --> 00:55:57.866 line:80%
Okay. We'll be right there.

00:55:57.950 --> 00:55:59.576 line:80%
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

00:56:00.786 --> 00:56:03.288 line:80%
Hey, they're asking for a script meeting.
Okay? Come on.

00:56:03.372 --> 00:56:05.165 line:80%
[Chan in Korean]
<i>We didn't want to give up, no matter what,</i>

00:56:05.249 --> 00:56:08.961 line:80%
<i>so we all fought through it</i>
<i>with gritted teeth.</i>

00:56:09.044 --> 00:56:12.006 line:80%
We agreed to revise the parts
that had differing opinions.

00:56:12.089 --> 00:56:14.550 line:80%
-[♪ music fades]
-[sighs] That's such a relief.

00:56:14.633 --> 00:56:16.510 line:80%
You said you worked on it
for over two years.

00:56:16.593 --> 00:56:18.178 line:80%
That's one thing…

00:56:18.262 --> 00:56:19.263 line:80%
Mmm…

00:56:21.181 --> 00:56:23.767 line:80%
But I really wanted to apply Won's costume

00:56:24.351 --> 00:56:27.563 line:80%
that you made in the animation.

00:56:28.731 --> 00:56:31.942 line:80%
And that's what got me through it.

00:56:37.614 --> 00:56:40.576 line:80%
Let's eat up and go.
Mr. Park's been waiting for you.

00:56:40.659 --> 00:56:42.745 line:80%
I want to spend more time with you.

00:56:44.163 --> 00:56:45.748 line:80%
Can you stay out late tonight?

00:56:53.172 --> 00:56:55.466 line:80%
I'll clear the table
and bring your dessert.

00:56:55.549 --> 00:56:56.550 line:80%
Thank you.

00:56:56.633 --> 00:56:59.261 line:80%
[Chan inhales sharply]
I should call Mr. Park.

00:56:59.345 --> 00:57:00.346 line:80%
[Chan sighs]

00:57:01.930 --> 00:57:03.682 line:80%
[line connects, rings]

00:57:04.099 --> 00:57:05.184 line:80%
Mr. Park, I'm here.

00:57:05.267 --> 00:57:08.103 line:80%
-[Manjae sobbing] <i>Genius, Chan is here!</i>
-[Genius barks]

00:57:08.187 --> 00:57:10.064 line:80%
-Why are you crying?
-He's crying?

00:57:11.357 --> 00:57:13.067 line:80%
I'm sorry I couldn't call.

00:57:13.150 --> 00:57:15.110 line:80%
No, no. It's fine. [sniffles]

00:57:15.194 --> 00:57:17.863 line:80%
[sobbing] I'm just so happy.

00:57:17.946 --> 00:57:20.032 line:80%
I thought I'd never see you again.

00:57:20.783 --> 00:57:22.743 line:80%
I was so upset.

00:57:22.826 --> 00:57:24.620 line:80%
Don't cry.

00:57:24.703 --> 00:57:27.081 line:80%
Now I can finally sleep easy.

00:57:27.706 --> 00:57:29.208 line:80%
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:57:29.291 --> 00:57:30.626 line:80%
[sighs]

00:57:30.709 --> 00:57:31.877 line:80%
Yes.

00:57:33.671 --> 00:57:35.714 line:80%
Yes. All right.

00:57:40.010 --> 00:57:42.846 line:80%
Make sure to have dinner
and take your meds. I'll visit later.

00:57:43.472 --> 00:57:44.473 line:80%
Okay.

00:57:46.266 --> 00:57:47.601 line:80%
He was so excited, wasn't he?

00:57:49.144 --> 00:57:52.940 line:80%
[sighs] Mr. Park and the others
were waiting for you the whole time.

00:57:53.023 --> 00:57:58.153 line:80%
Our whole team, Genius,
and even Donggu came looking for you.

00:57:58.237 --> 00:58:01.532 line:80%
[Haran sighs in relief]
I'm so glad everything worked out.

00:58:02.241 --> 00:58:04.702 line:80%
[sighs] Only good things
will happen from now on.

00:58:04.785 --> 00:58:05.786 line:80%
For real.

00:58:06.954 --> 00:58:09.665 line:80%
[Haran sighs in relief]
Everything's going to be fine now.

00:58:10.332 --> 00:58:11.667 line:80%
Everything's fine.

00:58:15.963 --> 00:58:17.381 line:80%
[inhales sharply]

00:58:38.068 --> 00:58:39.570 line:20%
JAY YOON 2ND EXHIBIT

00:58:47.077 --> 00:58:50.748 line:80%
[Manjae] <i>I missed you too,</i>
<i>but Haran would've had quite a hard time.</i>

00:58:51.498 --> 00:58:53.834 line:80%
<i>You're the one</i>
<i>who gave her the camera, right?</i>

00:58:53.917 --> 00:58:58.130 line:80%
<i>She seemed so excited</i>
<i>when she was taking the photos,</i>

00:58:58.213 --> 00:59:00.966 line:80%
<i>but after you left,</i>
<i>her eyes were always bloodshot</i>

00:59:01.050 --> 00:59:03.594 line:80%
<i>as if she wasn't sleeping well.</i>

00:59:27.201 --> 00:59:28.202 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

00:59:31.455 --> 00:59:34.541 line:80%
We'll do this line.

00:59:34.625 --> 00:59:35.918 line:80%
Please send us an email.

00:59:36.001 --> 00:59:37.002 line:80%
All right.

00:59:37.670 --> 00:59:40.297 line:80%
But is business not going well these days?

00:59:40.381 --> 00:59:41.674 line:80%
Our company?

00:59:41.757 --> 00:59:46.553 line:80%
Mr. Yeon came by in person yesterday,
so I wondered if anything's wrong.

00:59:46.637 --> 00:59:49.765 line:80%
Why would he come here in person?

00:59:49.848 --> 00:59:52.184 line:80%
He always paid upfront
when placing orders,

00:59:52.267 --> 00:59:54.812 line:80%
but this time, he asked to pay afterward,

00:59:54.895 --> 00:59:56.897 line:80%
saying he needed new materials.

00:59:56.981 --> 00:59:58.273 line:80%
New materials…

00:59:59.692 --> 01:00:01.485 line:80%
-Was it…
-Bio-silk.

01:00:01.568 --> 01:00:02.861 line:80%
Fermented protein fabric.

01:00:06.657 --> 01:00:10.619 line:80%
<i>He said he didn't want money</i>
<i>to limit the designers' creativity.</i>

01:00:10.703 --> 01:00:13.831 line:80%
<i>He asked us to get the material,</i>
<i>no matter what.</i>

01:00:13.914 --> 01:00:15.582 line:80%
<i>It's been 10 years,</i>

01:00:15.666 --> 01:00:18.127 line:80%
<i>but I've never seen him</i>
<i>ask for something so earnestly.</i>

01:00:19.712 --> 01:00:20.838 line:80%
[line connects]

01:00:21.422 --> 01:00:24.883 line:80%
-Mr. Yeon, where are you?
-[Taeseok] <i>I'm on my way to a meeting.</i>

01:00:29.096 --> 01:00:31.056 line:80%
Wait! Stop!

01:00:31.974 --> 01:00:33.892 line:80%
[pants, huffs]

01:00:34.893 --> 01:00:36.562 line:80%
[pants]

01:00:36.645 --> 01:00:40.316 line:80%
You rejected the idea at the meeting.
Why would you beg someone else to help?

01:00:40.983 --> 01:00:41.984 line:80%
What…

01:00:43.527 --> 01:00:44.611 line:80%
Ah.

01:00:45.362 --> 01:00:47.281 line:80%
-I only focus on reality during meetings.
-[sighs]

01:00:47.364 --> 01:00:49.491 line:80%
If I say it's possible
and it turns out it's not,

01:00:49.575 --> 01:00:52.828 line:80%
the designers will end up
dealing with the consequences.

01:00:52.911 --> 01:00:54.997 line:80%
You made me seem like an immature kid.

01:00:56.123 --> 01:01:00.002 line:80%
If I'd known, I wouldn't have gone on
about all that protein fabric.

01:01:01.337 --> 01:01:04.840 line:80%
It's okay, so you don't have
to go through all that trouble.

01:01:04.923 --> 01:01:07.384 line:80%
It's really, really fine with me.

01:01:07.468 --> 01:01:11.096 line:80%
So don't go anywhere pleading for help.

01:01:11.180 --> 01:01:12.598 line:80%
Why are you…

01:01:14.141 --> 01:01:15.726 line:80%
always saying you're okay?

01:01:17.227 --> 01:01:19.104 line:80%
This is why I didn't tell you.

01:01:20.272 --> 01:01:23.025 line:80%
I knew you'd say you're okay
when you're not.

01:01:25.152 --> 01:01:27.196 line:80%
It's my job to take care of such issues.

01:01:27.279 --> 01:01:29.615 line:80%
So you can be greedy about what you want

01:01:31.200 --> 01:01:32.993 line:80%
and tell people…

01:01:34.036 --> 01:01:35.371 line:80%
you're not okay

01:01:36.872 --> 01:01:37.873 line:80%
when you're not.

01:01:44.880 --> 01:01:46.757 line:80%
What…

01:01:51.762 --> 01:01:56.058 line:80%
When did I keep saying I was okay?

01:01:58.852 --> 01:02:02.523 line:80%
-[♪ sentimental music playing]
-[young Haran crying]

01:02:08.445 --> 01:02:10.572 line:80%
[young Haran] Mom…

01:02:14.410 --> 01:02:16.578 line:80%
-[young Haran continues crying]
-[sniffling]

01:02:22.209 --> 01:02:23.752 line:80%
I have to be okay.

01:02:25.295 --> 01:02:27.089 line:80%
I have to keep our family together.

01:02:29.049 --> 01:02:30.342 line:80%
[breathing shakily]

01:02:31.552 --> 01:02:33.012 line:80%
I have to be okay.

01:02:33.679 --> 01:02:36.181 line:80%
I have to be okay. [breathes deeply]

01:02:41.186 --> 01:02:42.396 line:80%
Mr. Yeon.

01:02:44.273 --> 01:02:45.399 line:80%
I'm sorry.

01:02:46.775 --> 01:02:48.444 line:80%
Why are you sorry?

01:02:49.111 --> 01:02:50.904 line:80%
You're the first one to come here.

01:02:51.488 --> 01:02:53.782 line:80%
Go and say goodbye to Mom and Dad.

01:02:53.866 --> 01:02:54.867 line:80%
I'm sorry.

01:02:56.452 --> 01:02:57.578 line:80%
I'm really sorry.

01:03:06.587 --> 01:03:07.588 line:80%
[♪ music fades]

01:03:07.671 --> 01:03:09.923 line:80%
I can't believe
I slept for an hour at a restaurant.

01:03:10.007 --> 01:03:11.175 line:80%
You should've woken me.

01:03:11.884 --> 01:03:14.928 line:80%
Huh? Wasn't that restaurant your home?

01:03:15.012 --> 01:03:17.222 line:80%
You slept so comfortably,
I thought it was your house.

01:03:17.306 --> 01:03:20.684 line:80%
[sighs] I slept while you're the one
who took a 10-hour flight.

01:03:20.768 --> 01:03:22.519 line:80%
Go home and get some sleep.

01:03:22.603 --> 01:03:24.730 line:80%
No, I'm wide awake now.

01:03:24.813 --> 01:03:28.901 line:80%
But didn't you come from the airport?
Where's all your luggage?

01:03:28.984 --> 01:03:30.110 line:80%
What luggage?

01:03:30.194 --> 01:03:31.320 line:80%
[♪ whimsical music playing]

01:03:31.403 --> 01:03:32.655 line:80%
My suitcase!

01:03:32.738 --> 01:03:35.199 line:80%
DEPARTURE TEAM 1

01:03:41.330 --> 01:03:44.833 line:80%
All your important stuff must be in there.
How could you forget a whole bag?

01:03:44.917 --> 01:03:47.836 line:80%
I was just in a hurry to make it on time.

01:03:47.920 --> 01:03:49.588 line:80%
Don't worry.

01:03:49.672 --> 01:03:53.592 line:80%
The lost and found system's pretty good,
so I'm sure I'll find it.

01:03:53.676 --> 01:03:56.720 line:80%
Sir, please stop
in front of the coffee-colored gate.

01:03:57.846 --> 01:03:59.056 line:80%
Tell me when you find it.

01:03:59.139 --> 01:04:02.434 line:80%
Don't wait up for me.
I'll leave you a message if I find it.

01:04:02.518 --> 01:04:04.478 line:80%
[inhales sharply] Uh…

01:04:05.020 --> 01:04:07.690 line:80%
You might fall asleep in the yard
on the way inside.

01:04:07.773 --> 01:04:10.901 line:80%
[chuckles softly]
I'll go to SHIM tomorrow morning.

01:04:10.985 --> 01:04:13.445 line:80%
Okay. I'll see you tomorrow, then.

01:04:19.743 --> 01:04:21.286 line:80%
What a shame.

01:04:25.040 --> 01:04:26.041 line:80%
[chuckles softly]

01:04:26.125 --> 01:04:28.127 line:80%
[indistinct chatter]

01:04:29.878 --> 01:04:30.879 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

01:04:30.963 --> 01:04:33.757 line:20%
[sighs in relief] I found it.

01:04:33.841 --> 01:04:35.926 line:20%
DESIGNER SONG HARAN

01:04:36.010 --> 01:04:37.177 line:20%
I'll see you tomorrow.

01:04:38.012 --> 01:04:40.014 line:80%
[cell phone vibrating]

01:04:41.598 --> 01:04:44.476 line:80%
[exclaims teasingly]
I told you not to wait up.

01:04:44.560 --> 01:04:47.271 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Did you check your stuff?</i>
<i>Is everything inside?</i>

01:04:47.354 --> 01:04:48.355 line:80%
Yes, I checked…

01:04:52.484 --> 01:04:54.486 line:80%
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:04:56.071 --> 01:04:57.239 line:80%
That's great.

01:05:03.787 --> 01:05:06.582 line:80%
Didn't you say you hated the first snow?

01:05:06.665 --> 01:05:07.833 line:80%
[Haran] <i>The first snow?</i>

01:05:07.916 --> 01:05:12.671 line:80%
[Haran sighs] <i>I did, but I feel like</i>
<i>I'll start hating it less now.</i>

01:05:12.755 --> 01:05:13.839 line:80%
<i>But why do you ask?</i>

01:05:15.341 --> 01:05:19.178 line:80%
You said you hated it,
but you're wandering about outside.

01:05:19.261 --> 01:05:21.180 line:80%
[Haran] <i>Do you even know where I am?</i>

01:05:21.889 --> 01:05:23.307 line:80%
<i>Can you see me?</i>

01:05:24.141 --> 01:05:25.142 line:80%
<i>Where are you?</i>

01:05:25.643 --> 01:05:27.728 line:80%
You said you were home…

01:05:27.811 --> 01:05:29.521 line:80%
I thought I'd regret it.

01:05:30.356 --> 01:05:31.732 line:80%
[Haran pants]

01:05:32.358 --> 01:05:36.570 line:80%
After you suddenly disappeared,
I had a lot of regrets.

01:05:37.196 --> 01:05:41.450 line:80%
[panting] I kept remembering how harsh
I was on you when you were so nice to me.

01:05:41.533 --> 01:05:42.534 line:80%
[♪ music ends]

01:05:43.577 --> 01:05:47.748 line:80%
<i>I don't want to have any more regrets,</i>
<i>so can you help me out?</i>

01:05:47.831 --> 01:05:49.833 line:80%
[panting]

01:05:53.128 --> 01:05:58.050 line:80%
Is it okay if I be really nice
to you this time?

01:05:59.134 --> 01:06:01.136 line:80%
-[♪ slow romantic song playing]
-[sighs]

01:06:04.056 --> 01:06:05.516 line:80%
<i>I'll start today.</i>

01:06:06.016 --> 01:06:08.435 line:80%
I'll keep you company on the way to Seoul.

01:06:10.270 --> 01:06:12.606 line:80%
But where are you?

01:06:14.233 --> 01:06:15.234 line:80%
I found you.

01:06:15.609 --> 01:06:16.694 line:80%
[chuckles]

01:06:18.070 --> 01:06:19.154 line:80%
[sighs softly]

01:06:24.243 --> 01:06:25.285 line:80%
This is bad.

01:06:26.704 --> 01:06:28.163 line:80%
What? What's bad?

01:06:28.747 --> 01:06:30.874 line:80%
[Chan] <i>I've been holding back until now…</i>

01:06:32.376 --> 01:06:36.422 line:80%
<i>I can't even explain myself to you,</i>

01:06:37.548 --> 01:06:41.135 line:80%
<i>and I shouldn't like you this much.</i>

01:06:42.386 --> 01:06:45.306 line:80%
-Your bag…
-[Chan] <i>I shouldn't keep wanting you…</i>

01:06:45.389 --> 01:06:48.183 line:80%
-You should bring…
<i>-…like this…</i>

01:06:50.144 --> 01:06:52.479 line:80%
[♪ song continues]

01:07:20.090 --> 01:07:21.175 line:80%
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:07:21.258 --> 01:07:22.718 line:20%
[♪ song continues]

01:07:45.282 --> 01:07:47.368 line:20%
[Haran] <i>He spoke as if he knew me.</i>

01:07:47.451 --> 01:07:52.164 line:20%
[Chan] <i>I may not be as good</i>
<i>for Designer Song.</i>

01:07:52.247 --> 01:07:53.957 line:20%
You used to call him Chan.

01:07:54.041 --> 01:07:57.169 line:20%
<i>Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.</i>

01:07:57.252 --> 01:07:59.505 line:20%
[Haran] <i>Their names… were similar.</i>

01:08:00.339 --> 01:08:02.966 line:20%
[Nana] <i>How much do you know</i>
<i>about Haran's past?</i>

01:08:03.050 --> 01:08:06.553 line:20%
[Chan] <i>I'm sorry for leaving like that</i>
<i>and for hurting you.</i>

01:08:07.304 --> 01:08:09.264 line:20%
[Manjae] <i>Why is this pen here?</i>

01:08:09.348 --> 01:08:12.726 line:20%
[Chan] <i>If I just play dumb</i>
<i>and be greedy until I go back,</i>

01:08:12.810 --> 01:08:14.937 line:20%
<i>would that be wrong?</i>

